-- experiments/nbe/p26-wip.cub — work in progress (2026-11-12): the rebuild of lib/nbe.cub's judgments
-- over cubes (P2.6d, P2.6e begun), as a working copy of lib/nbe.cub. Load in place of lib/nbe.cub:
--   ./build/cubical lib/prelude.cub lib/code.cub lib/match.cub lib/nav.cub lib/cost.cub lib/lin.cub
--     lib/check.cub lib/std.cub experiments/nbe/p26-wip.cub
-- (not with lib/nbe.cub, whose names it reuses; experiments/nbe/examples.cub does not load on it).
-- What it contains: lib/nbe.cub at d307c8a with P1's families and everything built on them removed
-- (PTy, Ctx/Env/ext, Jdg, VarT/Var, NN, Der, TCode, Ren, ren-nn, CompS, Comp, comp-ren, reify/reflect,
-- rr, CompEnv, env-ren, var-comp, case-comp, fund, reflect-env, embed, normalize, reifySound,
-- normalize-sound), the shape s-path added to TyShape (TyE's clause is PathS/PathE written out), and
-- appended: P2.6d (sem-path; Jdg over CCtx; the rule data AppV, CaseV and their projections app-f,
-- app-a, app-r, sig-1, sig-2, case-x, case-t, case-f, case-r, bool-v; lam-dom, lam-ctx, lam-body;
-- plam-line, plam-body; carry; papp-mean; PathM (t52); NN with nvar, napp, nfst, nsnd, ncase, nne,
-- ntrue, nfalse, nlam, npair, nplam, npapp; Der likewise with dpapp; TCode, teval, embed) and P2.6e
-- begun (cube-const, dcube-const, CMap, cmap-cube, cmap-d, SubF, sub-base, Sub, sub-carried,
-- sub-pull, subM, cmap-zero; then item (3) of the next definitions: fmap-const, fmap-cmap,
-- pull-fmap, subM-fmap; then (2026-11-12, later) item (1) entire (renaming of forms, OPE as closed
-- data, canon-ren, nonconst-ren), item (4) on cubes (ope-cube, ope-nat, diag-ren, papp-ren) and item
-- (2) on cubes (cmap-of, cmap-skip, cmap-keep, cmap-id, cmap-ope); then (2026-11-12, latest) (2d)
-- entire (the dependent forms over cubes: pcat-d … cmap-ope-d) and (2s) in part (sub-id, sub-wk,
-- sub-dwk, papp-nat, cmap-nat, sub-form, carry-fill, dmap-const-cube, map-pull).
-- What checks: all of it (run 2026-11-12 with CUBICAL_NOCACHE=1: "497 passed, 0 failed").
-- What is next: the dated next-definitions list at the end of lib/nbe.cub's head (2026-11-12,
-- "P2.6e from p26-wip"), then the swap of this file's families into lib/nbe.cub in place of P1's.

-- lib/nbe.cub — typed codes Code(Γ, A) = Σ c. Der(Γ, c, A) over the one representation of terms
-- (lib/code.cub's Code), their evaluation, and normalization by evaluation with its soundness
-- equation (paper §6.1, (6.1) and (6.5)). Loaded after lib/std.cub.
--
-- Status (2026-11-12, latest first).
-- * Step 1 (levels) done and checked: P1 rebuilt with types as maps into semantic types (below), the
--   semantic types and environments in Type 1 and the meanings of P1's shapes in Type, every level
--   closed. normalize, reifySound and normalize-sound still hold by refl.
-- * P2 (paths and the interval) in progress, checked so far: lines and cubes with the cube category's
--   generators and their laws, cube-comp/cube-id/dcube-map-of as paths, dependent cubes, canonical
--   forms of interval codes and path application on cubes at them, skeletons with dimension entries,
--   the semantic PathP type, and (P2.6 foundation) the structural maps of cubes over cubes, path
--   application on them, and papp-deg. Not yet built: the judgments, normal forms, derivations,
--   computability and normalization over cubes (P2.6a–e), which type derivations and their
--   computability (P2.5) need first; then P3 (Kan operations), P4 (Glue), P6 (universes). The exact
--   next definitions are the dated list at the end of this head.
--
-- Finding (2026-11-12) that replaces the level design "meanings in Type (lvl s)" (P6's design below,
-- and step 1 as first stated), for a theoretical reason. The derivation and normal-form families
-- quantify, in their constructors, over shapes whose meanings' levels vary (application quantifies
-- over the domain's shape, whose meaning may be in Type 1 while the result's is in Type), and the
-- Kripke clause of computability quantifies over all contexts, whose environments' levels vary with
-- their entries. A type containing such a quantification lives at no finite level: it needs a
-- universe above all levels (Agda's Setω) or cumulativity, and the core has neither (data at a level
-- depending on a variable is refused, E-openlevel). (While this was found the checker read a stuck
-- level as lzero and so would have accepted the design; that was t51, closed 2026-11-12 by the
-- coordinator: a stuck level is now an atom.) The design that holds in the core, with nothing lifted
-- (El of a code still the top-level type judgmentally): every level a field or a Kripke
-- quantification mentions is closed. Environments and semantic types are in one fixed universe,
-- Type 1 (the empty environment is One1); the meanings of a shape are in a closed universe fixed by
-- its stratum: P1's shapes mean types in Type; P6 adds the stratum whose meanings are in Type 1 (the
-- universe U_0, whose El is Type). What must be repeated per stratum, and why, is exactly: (i) a data
-- constructor (of shapes, normal forms, derivations) for each closed combination of the strata of the
-- meanings its fields mention, because a data type's fields must have closed levels and a meaning's
-- level is closed only when its stratum is (Π of a stratum-0 domain and a stratum-1 codomain has
-- meanings in lmax 0 1, which is closed; Π of shapes a, b of unknown strata has lmax (lvl a) (lvl b),
-- which is not); (ii) the clause of each shape-recursive function (Sem, El, CompS, rr, fund) at those
-- constructors. Each such constructor's type and each such clause is a one-line instance, at closed
-- levels, of one helper abstracted over level variables (which the checker treats as atoms): the rule
-- (its premises and conclusion as functions of the meanings) is written once. Everything else —
-- contexts (CtxE gets one clause per entry stratum, Env stays in Type 1 since lmax 1 0 and lmax 1 1
-- are closed), worlds, renaming, environments, the Kripke structure — is written once. Not yet
-- tested: whether a constructor's type may be given as a defined rule type applied to closed levels
-- (else each constructor's telescope is written out, still one line per combination over the
-- helpers). A second universe U_1 is a further stratum, the same way.
--
-- Decision (2026-11-12, step 1): a type of shape s over environments G is a map T : G → Sem s into
-- the semantic types of shape s (Sem s-bool = One1, Sem (Π a b) = Sem (Σ a b) = Fam a b = (A : Sem a)
-- × (El a A → Sem b)), its meaning El s (T ρ), Sem and El one pair by recursion on the closed shape.
-- This replaces the closures (a base K, a map into it, a structure over K): pulling back is still
-- composition and the meanings still compute at open environments by the shape's clause, but a type
-- is one map instead of a base, a map and a structure, so every rule takes one argument T where it
-- took K, g, A, B.
--
-- P2's design (2026-11-12, decided by the criterion that meanings are the language's own types
-- judgmentally, with no conversion paths). The interval as a higher inductive type is ruled out:
-- its paths are maps out of that type, equivalent to PathP only up to paths. A dimension entry
-- contributing "(i : I) → …" to curried meanings is not available either, and for a theoretical
-- reason: CCHM has no Π over the interval (I is not a type, and its only abstraction is PathP); the
-- implementation agrees (`fI : (i : I) → Bool` is refused, "code: not a bound variable or checked
-- definition: I", run 2026-11-12). So a dimension contributes a PathP whose endpoints are bound in a
-- Σ: an n-dimensional judgment is a cube (Cube n X: two (n-1)-cubes and a PathP between them) and
-- its meaning a section (Sec n T); checked below (sec1-pathp: a 1-section's path is the language's
-- PathP, by refl). The endpoints are redundant but judgmentally equal to the path's own (p 0 ≡ c0).
-- What P2 then is: P1's Jdg, NN, Der, Comp, rr and fund over cubes of contexts and types, P1 being
-- the case n = 0 (one construction, refactored, not a second copy); dimension expressions (0, 1,
-- the n bound dimensions, ~, ∧, ∨) acting on sections by recursion on n inside PathP-λ; the Kripke
-- worlds extended from renamings to the cube category's maps (faces, degeneracies, connections,
-- reversal), which is Sterling–Angiuli's setting.
-- Refinement (2026-11-12): what varies along a dimension is the context's entries' types, the type
-- and the meaning (γ, T, v); the skeleton, the shape and the code do not, and must not be inside the
-- cube: a path in a closed data type (Lst Entry, TyShape, Code) is not judgmentally constant, so
-- CtxE and TyE would be stuck along it. So the cube is Cube n (JV sk s) for the fixed skeleton sk,
-- shape s and code, JV sk s = (γ : fst (CtxE sk)) × (T : Env (sk , γ) → Sem s) × meanings. Operations
-- on cubes are defined by recursion on n applied to `p i` under a path λ (a function cannot take an
-- interval point, but it can be applied to the cube p i), so faces, degeneracies, reversal,
-- connections, exchange and the diagonal at any depth are functions Cube n X → Cube m X.
--
-- Finding (2026-11-12, P2): compositions of cube operations at a variable dimension are not
-- judgmental. `cube-map n f (cube-map n g c)` against `cube-map n (λ x → f (g x)) c` by refl is refused
-- at a variable n ("wrong endpoint at 0": cube-map is stuck on n); it holds as a path by induction
-- (cube-comp below). So in a cube-indexed family the index a constructor computes and the one a
-- generic definition (reify, renaming, fund) needs agree only up to such paths, and the value is
-- transported along them (a forded family's transport computes on constructors). The meaning of a
-- typed code is stored apart from its derivation (TCode's v), so reifySound and normalize-sound stay
-- refl; what is lost beyond n = 0 is only that a normal form's index is its input's by construction.
-- Ruled out, with reasons: (a) meanings as functions of lines of environments (a λ after a dimension
-- needs its body pointwise, which a function of a whole line cannot give); (b) derivations in a
-- context with a dimension as host paths of P1 derivations (a neutral p @ i is neutral inside and its
-- endpoint's normal form at the boundary, which a uniform path λ cannot be, and the code's dimension
-- index would not be tied to the host's dimension); (c) a fixed base cube with pointwise maps (the
-- free functor form, where composition is judgmental): a dimension-dependent term such as p @ j is
-- not a function of the point, so bases change at it and zips at a variable dimension return.
-- Needed by P2 and absent from P1: type derivations with codes (a PathP type has endpoint terms;
-- reflecting a neutral of path type at a constant dimension needs the endpoints' computability, and
-- P3's neutral comp contains the normal form of a line of types), so computability of types (CompTy,
-- by recursion on the shape) with reify/reflect taking it. Worlds in P2 are renamings including
-- weakening by a dimension: no P2 rule substitutes a constant or a compound expression for a world's
-- dimension (path application interprets its expression by the cube operations below, and
-- computability at PathP is Kripke over the dimension expressions of later worlds, so a neutral p @ r
-- is formed only at a non-constant r in normal form). Faces, connections and reversal as world maps
-- enter with systems in P3, with Sterling–Angiuli's stabilization; as operations on meanings they
-- are below.
--
-- P6's design (2026-11-12; its level part is replaced by the finding above, its universe part
-- stands). A universe's shape means Type ℓ; a type given by an element t of a universe has the shape
-- s-el whose meaning is t's meaning itself (El t is the top-level type judgmentally). Reify at a
-- universe needs a code for a value that is a Type, which cannot be inspected, so computability at
-- U_ℓ carries one (as in Sterling–Angiuli's glued universe): a code of level ℓ, its normal form, and a
-- path in Type ℓ from its meaning to the value; computability at s-el is computability at that code,
-- transported along the path (a predicate on values, not a conversion rule of the object theory). Its
-- recursion is on the level first (the strata), then the shape (an s-el at level ℓ+1 names a code of
-- level ℓ), all on closed skeletons.
--
-- Plan (2026-11-12). The whole construction, in the order it is built.
--
-- 0. Source of the method. Kripke normalization by evaluation for dependent types with a logical
--    relation (computability) over the category of contexts and order-preserving renamings: the
--    method of Altenkirch–Kaposi (LMCS 2017) and Coquand ("Canonicity and normalization for
--    dependent type theory", TCS 2019), and for the cubical part Sterling–Angiuli (LICS 2021).
--    The derivations are indexed by their meaning (McBride, "Outrageous but meaningful
--    coincidences", 2010): a derivation of c : A in Γ carries, as an index, the meaning of c as a
--    function of the environment. So eval is that index, the object theory's conversion is the
--    language's own judgmental equality on meanings (no conversion rule, nothing to make coherent),
--    and (6.5) holds by the indices.
--
-- 1. Objects, each defined once.
--    Raw     the existing Code (lib/code.cub); normal forms here use cvar, clam, capp, cpair, cfst,
--            csnd, ccase #0 (Bool), ccon #0 k, cplam, cpapp — the codes the language's own (code t)
--            writes for the same terms.
--    Types   a shape (TyShape, closed data) and a map from the environments into Sem of the shape
--            (step 1, above).
--    Ctx     a context: a skeleton (list of shapes, closed data) with each entry's type; its
--            environment type is computed by recursion on the skeleton.
--    Var, Der  variables and typing derivations, Der Γ D c v: c is a derivation-checked raw code
--            of type D in Γ with meaning v : (ρ : G) → T ρ.
--    Code Γ D = Σ c. Σ v. Der Γ D c v; eval = the meaning v (paper (6.1)).
--    Ne, Nf  neutral and normal derivations, same indices; embed : Nf → Der keeps c and v.
--    Worlds  renamings Δ → Γ (functions on variables with their meaning map), with actions on Ne, Nf.
--    Comp s Δ T x  the computability of x : (ρ : Env Δ) → El s (T ρ) at world Δ, by recursion on s:
--            Bool — true, false or a neutral; Π — Kripke: at every later world, computable
--            arguments give computable results; Σ — componentwise.
--    reify/reflect  mutually by recursion on the shape: reify : Comp → Σ c. Nf with meaning exactly
--            x; reflect : Ne → Comp. The Π clauses are the paper's Kripke clauses (§6.1).
--    fund    the fundamental lemma, by recursion on Der: a derivation's meaning is computable at
--            every world under every computable environment.
--    normalize d = reify (fund d (reflected identity environment)); the result is a Code with the
--            same meaning index, so reifySound (6.5) is refl: eval (reify v) ρ ≡ denote v ρ.
--
-- 2. Phases. P1 the fragment Π, Σ, Bool (with dependent case): done. Step 1 (closed levels, types
--    as maps into semantic types): done. P2 PathP and the interval: worlds with dimension variables
--    and face restrictions (Comp at a path type is computability of every dimension instance, with
--    the boundary). P3 Kan operations, transp and hcomp, at Π, Σ, Bool, PathP: Sterling–Angiuli's
--    stabilization (neutrals carry the face on which they are unstable). P4 Glue. P5 the
--    specializer over Code (lib/specialize.cub's normalize, t11) — needs each definition reflected
--    into Der, which is the typed checker's output (goal typed-checker). P6 universes (above).
--
-- Correction (2026-11-12, replaces t45, closed; its lifting is in turn replaced by the finding at
-- the top): universes are not blocked and need nothing added to the core. The object hierarchy
-- U_0..U_k is finite. A `data ... : Type 1` annotation does not raise a level (a data type's level is
-- its fields' largest, t49).
--
-- Finding (2026-11-12) that fixes the design below: transport along a constant line of a variable
-- type does not reduce (CCHM has no regularity; `transport (λ i → A) a ≡ a` by refl is refused, while
-- at Bool it is accepted). The language's indexed families are forded (each index an equation field),
-- so a function defined by recursion over one computes its clauses only up to such transports when
-- the index involves variable types. Everything whose clauses must compute inside types (the meaning
-- of a type, computability, environments of a context) is therefore defined by recursion on closed
-- first-order skeletons (TyShape, lists of shapes), where clauses compute definitionally; indexed
-- families (derivations, normal forms) are only ever the arguments of functions whose result types
-- are fixed by their signatures, so the transports inside their results are harmless (their
-- indices, the meanings, are fixed by the types).
--
-- Elaborator quirk found 2026-11-12: in a structural recursion, an implicit binder after the recursive
-- argument is not abstracted in the induction hypothesis (the inner call gets the outer value, and an
-- explicit {..} is ignored); such parameters are taken explicitly here.
--
-- Decision (2026-11-12, P2.6, refines the cube form of judgments below): a judgment's cube is split
-- into a cube of contexts G : Cube (dims sk) (CtxV sk) and a cube over G of meanings, M : DCube
-- (dims sk) (CtxV sk) (λ γ → EnvV sk γ → Z) G (Z = TV s = (A : Sem s) × El s A for a term; a rule's
-- data for a rule). Reason: the plan's single cube of (γ, T, v) needs zips at a variable dimension
-- wherever two judgments over one context meet (weakening a judgment by a type that another judgment
-- supplies, reify Π's world), and zips agree with projections only up to paths; over one base cube G,
-- the maps between cubes over cubes (fmap, zip, reidx, push, pull, the generators' lifts, papp-cube-d,
-- below) are structural, with no path. What remains up to paths: composites of these maps (the
-- naturality lemmas listed below), and carrying a cube over a base along a path of bases (papp-deg;
-- a substitution's base equation).
-- Finding (2026-11-12, P2.6): the fundamental lemma needs substitutions with explicit environment
-- maps, not worlds given as functions on cubes (P1's Ren style). In fund (dlam) the substitution for
-- the body is the given one, then the Kripke world, extended by the argument cube Y; acting on a
-- meaning over the body's context needs each vertex's environment map, which a function on cubes
-- hides. So a substitution from Γ = (sk, G) to Δ = (sk', G') is a dimension part (a composite of
-- degeneracies, natural in the base type: Cube (dims sk) X → Cube (dims sk') X), a cube over G' of
-- pairs (γ : CtxV sk) × (EnvV sk' γ' → EnvV sk γ), and a path from the dimension part of G to that
-- cube's first projection; its action on meanings is reidx, then transport along the path, then
-- dcube-pull. Renamings (worlds) are the substitutions whose entries are variables; their action on
-- normal forms is ren-nn as in P1, transported along the action's naturality.
--
-- Next definitions (2026-11-12, latest), in order. Done and checked: lines, cubes, generators,
-- cube-comp, cube-id; P2.4 (canonical interval forms, papp-cube); P2.2 (skeletons with dimension
-- entries, dims, CtxE/VarT/CompEnv/env-ren/var-comp/reflect-env with a dimension clause, ren-dim);
-- P2.1 (DCube, dcube-map, dcube-of, dcube-map-of); P2.3 (PathS/PathE); P2.6 foundation (bool-elim1,
-- pcat, psym, dcube-fmap/zip/reidx/push/pull, the generators over their images, papp-deg with
-- diag-deg … papp-dnf-from-deg, cube-comp2, papp-cube-d); P2.6a (CtxV, EnvV, FbE, CCtx, Mean, fmapM,
-- TV, extM, dext, wkM, dwkM); P2.6c (VarP, var-shape, var-word, varM, varCube: a variable is a
-- closed index into the skeleton, not P1's VarT); P2.6b (fmap-fmap, fmap-reidx, reidx-fmap,
-- fmap-push, push-fmap, fmap-pull, fmap-transp, and fmap∘papp-cube-d: fmap-gen, fmap-diag-sk …
-- fmap-papp).
-- (2026-11-12) P2.6d and P2.6e land in one commit: changing Jdg changes the index of NN and Der, so
-- ren-nn, CompS, rr, fund, embed, normalize and the P1 examples change with them, and building the
-- new families beside the old would be a second copy (not allowed). Rule data for P2.6d, each a
-- closed Type 1 read pointwise per environment, with the named projections shared by NN, Der, CompS
-- and reify: AppV a b = (T : Fam a b) × El (s-pi a b) T × El a (fst T), app-f q = (fst q , fst (snd
-- q)), app-a q = (fst (fst q) , snd (snd q)), app-r q = (snd (fst q) (snd (snd q)) , fst (snd q)
-- (snd (snd q))); for Σ, sig-1 (T , v) = (fst T , fst v) and sig-2 (T , v) = (snd T (fst v) , snd v)
-- (the premises of pair, the conclusions of fst and snd); CaseV sP = (B : One1) × (P : Bool → Sem
-- sP) × (x : Bool) × El sP (P true) × El sP (P false), scrutinee (B , x), branches (P true , t) and
-- (P false , f), result (P x , bool-elim (λ b → El sP (P b)) t f x); true/false: a cube B : Mean Γ
-- One1 and fmapM (λ u → (u , true)); var: varCube Γ v; lam: the conclusion X : Mean Γ (TV (s-pi a
-- b)), the body over extM Γ a (TV (s-pi a b)) (λ γ e ρ → fst (fst (e ρ))) X with meaning dcube-push
-- of X over X at (ρ , x) ↦ (snd (fst (e ρ)) x , snd (e ρ) x); plam: the conclusion X : Mean Γ (TV
-- (s-path a)), the body over dext Γ with meaning dcube-reidx at degen-l, each vertex's e read as the
-- line λ i ρ → (snd (snd (fst (fst (e ρ)))) i , snd (e ρ) i) with its two ends.
-- Tested 2026-11-12 (scratch file, not kept): a family indexed by (Γ : CCtx) × TyShape × Code × Mean Γ
-- (TV s), with a variable constructor at varCube and a projection constructor at fmapM, and
-- functions matching on it with the implicit index (as ren-nn and embed), check (0 failed).
--   P2.6a Contexts and meanings over cubes. CtxV sk = fst (CtxE sk), EnvV sk γ = snd (CtxE sk) γ;
--        CCtx = (sk : Lst Entry) × Cube (dims sk) (CtxV sk); Mean (Γ : CCtx) (Z : Type 1) = DCube
--        (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (λ γ → EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Z) (snd Γ); fmapM Γ Z Z' (h : Z → Z')
--        = dcube-fmap at λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ); TV s = (A : Sem s) × El s A. Extensions: by a type
--        given as a cube over G, extM Γ Y (f : (γ : CtxV sk) → (EnvV sk γ → Y) → EnvV sk γ → Sem a)
--        (M : Mean Γ Y) = (lcons (e-ty a) sk , dcube-map … (λ γ e → (γ , f γ e)) G M) (the context of a
--        λ's body is extM at its own conclusion cube, f the domain: no path); by a dimension, dext Γ
--        = (lcons e-dim sk , cube-map (dims sk) _ _ (degen-l _) G). Weakening of meanings: by
--        dcube-push (to extM) and dcube-reidx at degen-o (to dext).
--   P2.6b Naturality lemmas (paths, by induction on n): fmap∘fmap, fmap∘reidx, fmap∘push, fmap∘pull,
--        fmap∘papp-cube-d, and fmap commuting with transport along a path of bases (by a filler).
--   P2.6c Variables: VarS sk k s (index k names a term entry of shape s; closed, by recursion on sk)
--        and varM sk k p : (γ : CtxV sk) → EnvV sk γ → TV s; a variable's meaning is dcube-of of it.
--   P2.6d Judgments Jdg = (Γ : CCtx) × (s : TyShape) × Code × Mean Γ (TV s). NN and Der rebuilt
--        (replacing P1's, P1 the case dims = 0): each rule takes a cube R : Mean Γ (rule data) and
--        its premises' and conclusion's meanings are fmapM of named functions of the rule data (one
--        per rule, shared with CompS and reify). New: nplam/dplam (premise over dext Γ, meaning the
--        conclusion's reindexed at degen with the path read pointwise), npapp/dpapp (premise p over
--        Γ at a path type; fields a canonical form f, isTrue (dnf-canon f), and for npapp isTrue
--        (dnf-nonconst f); code cpapp p (dnf-code f); conclusion meaning Y with an equation field:
--        papp-cube-d at f of p's meaning reindexed at degen, carried along papp-deg G, is Y).
--   P2.5 (needs P2.6a–d) s-path in TyShape, TyE (s-path a) = (PathS (Sem a) (El a) , PathE (Sem a)
--        (El a)); DTy (Γ : CCtx) (s) (Code) (Mean Γ (Sem s)) with Bool, Π, Σ, PathP (line over dext
--        Γ, Der of both ends); CompTy by recursion on the shape (Bool One1; Π Kripke over
--        substitutions; Σ; PathP: CompTy of the line and CompS of both ends); fundTy.
--   P2.6e Substitutions Sub Δ Γ (the finding above), their action subM on meanings, the identity,
--        weakening by a type, by a dimension, extension by a cube of values; CompS s Δ x by recursion
--        on s (Bool: constantly true, constantly false (paths of meanings), or a neutral; Π: for
--        every renaming w : Δ' → Δ and Y : Mean Δ' (AppV a b) with a path from fmapM of its function
--        part to subM w x, CompS of its argument part gives CompS of its result; Σ componentwise;
--        PathP: for every renaming and every canonical form f over its target, CompS a of the path
--        applied at f, carried along papp-deg); comp-ren; rr (taking CompTy); CompEnv over a
--        substitution; fund; reflect-env; embed; normalize; reifySound and normalize-sound (refl on
--        TCode's stored meaning). Examples: ⟨i⟩ b to cplam (cvar #1); a path variable p to cplam
--        (cpapp (cvar #1) (cvar #0)); p @ 0 to the type's endpoint's normal form; P1's examples
--        unchanged.
--   P3, P4, P6 as in the plan above; P3 first extends worlds to the cube category (faces,
--        degeneracies, connections, reversal: the generators above), with neutrals carrying the face
--        on which they are unstable (Sterling–Angiuli), since systems substitute constants for a
--        world's dimensions.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- types: shapes and their semantic types
-- (2026-11-12, step 1) A type of shape s over environments G is a map from G into Sem s, the semantic
-- types of shape s; its meaning at ρ is El s (T ρ). Sem and El are defined together by recursion on
-- the closed shape (one pair, TyE, since mutual definitions by clauses are not available), so El of
-- an open semantic type computes by its shape's clause. Levels are closed everywhere (the finding at
-- the head): El s is
-- in Type (the stratum of P1's shapes; P6 adds the stratum whose meanings are in Type 1), Sem s and
-- environments are in Type 1, so a semantic type may contain a Type (the universe's El, P6) and an
-- environment may contain a type, with nothing lifted.
data TyShape = s-bool | s-pi (a : TyShape) (b : TyShape) | s-sig (a : TyShape) (b : TyShape) | s-path (a : TyShape)
-- the semantic Bool type: nothing; One1 is a type at level 1 with the one value `one`
data One1 = one1 (pad : Type → Type)
one : One1
one = one1 (λ X → X)
TyU : Type 2
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
TyU = (uM : Type 1) × (uM → Type)
-- binders hatted (Â D̂ x̂) because of t46 (telescope instantiation captures names)
TyE : TyShape → TyU
TyE s-bool = (One1 , λ D̂ → Bool)
TyE (s-pi a b) =
  ((Â : fst (TyE a)) × (snd (TyE a) Â → fst (TyE b)) ,
   λ D̂ → (x̂ : snd (TyE a) (fst D̂)) → snd (TyE b) (snd D̂ x̂))
TyE (s-sig a b) =
  ((Â : fst (TyE a)) × (snd (TyE a) Â → fst (TyE b)) ,
   λ D̂ → (x̂ : snd (TyE a) (fst D̂)) × snd (TyE b) (snd D̂ x̂))
-- (2026-11-12, P2.6d) the path shape: PathS/PathE (P2.3, below) written out, since TyE precedes them
-- (sem-path checks that they agree judgmentally)
TyE (s-path a) =
  ((pL̂ : (Â0 : fst (TyE a)) × (Â1 : fst (TyE a)) × PathP (λ i → fst (TyE a)) Â0 Â1) × snd (TyE a) (fst pL̂) × snd (TyE a) (fst (snd pL̂)) ,
   λ D̂ → PathP (λ i → snd (TyE a) (snd (snd (fst D̂)) i)) (fst (snd D̂)) (snd (snd D̂)))
Sem : TyShape → Type 1
Sem s = fst (TyE s)
El : (s : TyShape) → Sem s → Type
El s = snd (TyE s)
-- the semantic types of Π and Σ: a domain and a family over it (the same for both)
Fam : TyShape → TyShape → Type 1
Fam a b = (A : Sem a) × (El a A → Sem b)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- contexts
-- a context over a skeleton (its entries' shapes, closed data): the entries' types and the type of
-- its environments, by recursion on the skeleton; environments are in Type 1 (the empty one is One1)
-- (P2.2, 2026-11-12) A skeleton's entries are types' shapes or dimensions, newest first. A dimension
-- contributes nothing to a vertex's environment (its direction is the cube's, P2.6); codes count it
-- among the de Bruijn indices.
data Entry = e-ty (s : TyShape) | e-dim
dims : Lst Entry → Nat
dims lnil = zero
dims (lcons (e-ty s) sk) = dims sk
dims (lcons e-dim sk) = suc (dims sk)
CtxU : Type 2
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
CtxU = (uM : Type 1) × (uM → Type 1)
CtxE : Lst Entry → CtxU
CtxE lnil = (One1 , λ γ → One1)
CtxE (lcons e-dim sk) = CtxE sk
CtxE (lcons (e-ty s) sk) =
  ((γ : fst (CtxE sk)) × (snd (CtxE sk) γ → Sem s) ,
   λ p → (ρ : snd (CtxE sk) (fst p)) × El s (snd p ρ))
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- variables
-- the dependent eliminator of Bool, for the meanings of case
bool-elim : (P : Bool → Type) → P true → P false → (b : Bool) → P b
bool-elim P t f true = t
bool-elim P t f false = f

-- the kinds of the one family of neutral and normal forms; the codes of Bool's constructors and case
data NK = k-ne | k-nf
c-true : Code
c-true = ccon #0 #0 lnil lnil
c-false : Code
c-false = ccon #0 #1 lnil lnil
c-case : Code → Code → Code → Code
c-case t f x = ccase #0 (lcons t (lcons f lnil)) x

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2: lines and cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A line in X: two points and a path between them; its endpoints are the path's own
-- judgmentally (p 0 ≡ x0). An n-cube: an (n-1)-cube of lines, so the newest dimension is the
-- innermost and an n-cube of lines is literally an (n+1)-cube (a path λ's body, a PathP's meaning).
-- The interval enters only through PathP; operations are functions applied to `p i` under a path λ.
Line : Type 1 → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
Line X = (lx0 : X) × (lx1 : X) × PathP (λ i → X) lx0 lx1
Cube : Nat → Type 1 → Type 1
Cube zero X = X
Cube (suc n) X = Cube n (Line X)
line-map : (X Y : Type 1) → (X → Y) → Line X → Line Y
line-map X Y f L = (f (fst L) , f (fst (snd L)) , λ i → f (snd (snd L) i))
cube-map : (n : Nat) (X Y : Type 1) → (X → Y) → Cube n X → Cube n Y
cube-map zero X Y f c = f c
cube-map (suc n) X Y f c = cube-map n (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y f) c
-- the generators of the cube category at the newest dimension, on lines (an n-cube's are their
-- cube-maps): the two faces, the degeneracy, reversal, the connections ∧ and ∨, exchange of the two
-- newest dimensions and their diagonal
face0-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → X
face0-l X L = fst L
face1-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → X
face1-l X L = fst (snd L)
degen-l : (X : Type 1) → X → Line X
degen-l X x = (x , x , λ i → x)
rev-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → Line X
rev-l X L = (fst (snd L) , fst L , λ i → snd (snd L) (~ i))
-- λ i j → p (i ∧ j) and λ i j → p (i ∨ j) (j the newer)
meet-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → Line (Line X)
meet-l X L = ((fst L , fst L , λ j → fst L) , L , λ i → (fst L , snd (snd L) i , λ j → snd (snd L) (i ∧ j)))
join-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → Line (Line X)
join-l X L = (L , (fst (snd L) , fst (snd L) , λ j → fst (snd L)) , λ i → (snd (snd L) i , fst (snd L) , λ j → snd (snd L) (i ∨ j)))
-- λ i j → q j i
exch-l : (X : Type 1) → Line (Line X) → Line (Line X)
exch-l X Q =
  ((fst (fst Q) , fst (fst (snd Q)) , λ i → fst (snd (snd Q) i)) ,
   (fst (snd (fst Q)) , fst (snd (fst (snd Q))) , λ i → fst (snd (snd (snd Q) i))) ,
   λ j → (snd (snd (fst Q)) j , snd (snd (fst (snd Q))) j , λ i → snd (snd (snd (snd Q) i)) j))
-- λ i → q i i
diag-l : (X : Type 1) → Line (Line X) → Line X
diag-l X Q = (fst (fst Q) , fst (snd (fst (snd Q))) , λ i → snd (snd (snd (snd Q) i)) i)
-- their laws hold by refl (the endpoints of a path are its own judgmentally); the type is a line,
-- so the laws are PathPs (t50)
face0-degen : (X : Type 1) (x : X) → PathP (λ i → X) (face0-l X (degen-l X x)) x
face0-degen X x = λ i → x
rev-rev : (X : Type 1) (L : Line X) → PathP (λ i → Line X) (rev-l X (rev-l X L)) L
rev-rev X L = λ i → L
exch-exch : (X : Type 1) (Q : Line (Line X)) → PathP (λ i → Line (Line X)) (exch-l X (exch-l X Q)) Q
exch-exch X Q = λ i → Q
diag-degen : (X : Type 1) (L : Line X) → PathP (λ i → Line X) (diag-l X (degen-l (Line X) L)) L
diag-degen X L = λ i → L
diag-meet : (X : Type 1) (L : Line X) → PathP (λ i → Line X) (diag-l X (meet-l X L)) L
diag-meet X L = λ i → L
face1-meet : (X : Type 1) (L : Line X) → PathP (λ i → Line X) (face1-l (Line X) (meet-l X L)) L
face1-meet X L = λ i → L
-- composition of cube maps: at a variable dimension it does not hold by refl (refused, "wrong
-- endpoint at 0", 2026-11-12: cube-map is stuck on n); it holds as a path, by induction
cube-comp : (n : Nat) (X Y Z : Type 1) (f : Y → Z) (g : X → Y) (c : Cube n X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c)
cube-comp zero X Y Z f g c = λ i → f (g c)
cube-comp (suc n) X Y Z f g c = cube-comp n (Line X) (Line Y) (Line Z) (line-map Y Z f) (line-map X Y g) c
cube-id : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube n X) → PathP (λ i → Cube n X) (cube-map n X X (λ x → x) c) c
cube-id zero X c = λ i → c
cube-id (suc n) X c = cube-id n (Line X) c

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2: interval expressions, De Morgan normal forms
-- (2026-11-12) The interval of CCHM is the free De Morgan algebra on the dimension variables, which is
-- the free distributive lattice (with 0, 1) on the literals i and ~i; an element's canonical form is
-- an antichain of conjunctions of literals (a DNF with absorption), each conjunction a set of
-- literals. Interval expressions are the codes ci0, ci1, cvar k, cneg, cmeet, cjoin (the one code
-- representation); dnf-of reads one to its canonical form and dnf-code writes the form back. A
-- neutral path application is formed at a canonical, non-constant form only (P2.6), so that no normal
-- form applies a neutral path at an endpoint or at two spellings of one interval element.
-- a literal: a dimension variable and its polarity (true: i, false: ~i); ordered by variable, then ~i
-- before i
Lit : Type
Lit = Word × Bool
bool-eq : Bool → Bool → Bool
bool-eq true b = b
bool-eq false b = not b
lit-eq : Lit → Lit → Bool
lit-eq a b = andB (weq (fst a) (fst b)) (bool-eq (snd a) (snd b))
lit-lt : Lit → Lit → Bool
lit-lt a b = if wlt (fst a) (fst b) then true else (if weq (fst a) (fst b) then andB (not (snd a)) (snd b) else false)
-- a conjunction: a strictly increasing list of literals; a form: a list of conjunctions
Conj : Type
Conj = Lst Lit
DNF : Type
DNF = Lst Conj
-- the conjunction of two conjunctions (their union, as an ordered merge); by recursion on the first,
-- the second inserted literal by literal
conj-ins : Lit → Conj → Conj
conj-ins l lnil = lcons l lnil
conj-ins l (lcons m ms) = if lit-eq l m then lcons m ms else (if lit-lt l m then lcons l (lcons m ms) else lcons m (conj-ins l ms))
conj-meet : Conj → Conj → Conj
conj-meet lnil d = d
conj-meet (lcons l ls) d = conj-ins l (conj-meet ls d)
-- membership and inclusion
conj-has : Lit → Conj → Bool
conj-has l lnil = false
conj-has l (lcons m ms) = if lit-eq l m then true else conj-has l ms
conj-sub : Conj → Conj → Bool
conj-sub lnil d = true
conj-sub (lcons l ls) d = andB (conj-has l d) (conj-sub ls d)
-- equality of conjunctions as lists (a canonical conjunction is ordered, so this is set equality there)
conj-eq : Conj → Conj → Bool
conj-eq lnil lnil = true
conj-eq lnil (lcons m ms) = false
conj-eq (lcons l ls) lnil = false
conj-eq (lcons l ls) (lcons m ms) = andB (lit-eq l m) (conj-eq ls ms)
-- the order of conjunctions in a canonical form: shorter first, then by their first differing literal
conj-lt : Conj → Conj → Bool
conj-lt lnil lnil = false
conj-lt lnil (lcons m ms) = true
conj-lt (lcons l ls) lnil = false
conj-lt (lcons l ls) (lcons m ms) = if lit-lt l m then true else (if lit-eq l m then conj-lt ls ms else false)
-- adding a conjunction to a canonical form: dropped if some conjunction there is included in it
-- (absorption), else the ones that include it removed and it inserted in order
dnf-any-sub : Conj → DNF → Bool
dnf-any-sub c lnil = false
dnf-any-sub c (lcons d ds) = if conj-sub d c then true else dnf-any-sub c ds
dnf-drop-sup : Conj → DNF → DNF
dnf-drop-sup c lnil = lnil
dnf-drop-sup c (lcons d ds) = if conj-sub c d then dnf-drop-sup c ds else lcons d (dnf-drop-sup c ds)
dnf-insert : Conj → DNF → DNF
dnf-insert c lnil = lcons c lnil
dnf-insert c (lcons d ds) = if conj-lt c d then lcons c (lcons d ds) else lcons d (dnf-insert c ds)
dnf-add : Conj → DNF → DNF
dnf-add c f = if dnf-any-sub c f then f else dnf-insert c (dnf-drop-sup c f)
-- the lattice operations and De Morgan negation on canonical forms
dnf-join : DNF → DNF → DNF
dnf-join lnil g = g
dnf-join (lcons c cs) g = dnf-add c (dnf-join cs g)
dnf-meet-c : Conj → DNF → DNF
dnf-meet-c c lnil = lnil
dnf-meet-c c (lcons d ds) = dnf-add (conj-meet c d) (dnf-meet-c c ds)
dnf-meet : DNF → DNF → DNF
dnf-meet lnil g = lnil
dnf-meet (lcons c cs) g = dnf-join (dnf-meet-c c g) (dnf-meet cs g)
dnf-zero : DNF
dnf-zero = lnil
dnf-one : DNF
dnf-one = lcons lnil lnil
-- ~(l1 ∧ … ∧ lk) = ~l1 ∨ … ∨ ~lk, and ~(c1 ∨ … ∨ cm) = ~c1 ∧ … ∧ ~cm
neg-conj : Conj → DNF
neg-conj lnil = dnf-zero
neg-conj (lcons l ls) = dnf-add (lcons (fst l , not (snd l)) lnil) (neg-conj ls)
dnf-neg : DNF → DNF
dnf-neg lnil = dnf-one
dnf-neg (lcons c cs) = dnf-meet (neg-conj c) (dnf-neg cs)
-- an interval code's canonical form (none for a code that is not an interval expression)
dnf-of : Code → Opt DNF
dnf-of ci0 = some dnf-zero
dnf-of ci1 = some dnf-one
dnf-of (cvar k) = some (lcons (lcons (k , true) lnil) lnil)
dnf-of (cneg r) = case dnf-of r of none → none; some f → some (dnf-neg f)
dnf-of (cmeet r s) = case dnf-of r of none → none; some f → (case dnf-of s of none → none; some g → some (dnf-meet f g))
dnf-of (cjoin r s) = case dnf-of r of none → none; some f → (case dnf-of s of none → none; some g → some (dnf-join f g))
dnf-of c = none
-- a canonical form written as a code
lit-code : Lit → Code
lit-code l = if snd l then cvar (fst l) else cneg (cvar (fst l))
conj-code-from : Lit → Conj → Code
conj-code-from l lnil = lit-code l
conj-code-from l (lcons m ms) = cmeet (lit-code l) (conj-code-from m ms)
conj-code : Conj → Code
conj-code lnil = ci1
conj-code (lcons l ls) = conj-code-from l ls
dnf-code-from : Conj → DNF → Code
dnf-code-from c lnil = conj-code c
dnf-code-from c (lcons d ds) = cjoin (conj-code c) (dnf-code-from d ds)
dnf-code : DNF → Code
dnf-code lnil = ci0
dnf-code (lcons c cs) = dnf-code-from c cs
-- a form is canonical when it is its own normal form, and
-- constant when it is 0 or 1
dnf-eq : DNF → DNF → Bool
dnf-eq lnil lnil = true
dnf-eq lnil (lcons d ds) = false
dnf-eq (lcons c cs) lnil = false
dnf-eq (lcons c cs) (lcons d ds) = andB (conj-eq c d) (dnf-eq cs ds)
-- the normal form of any list of conjunctions: each conjunction ordered, then all added
dnf-norm : DNF → DNF
dnf-norm lnil = lnil
dnf-norm (lcons c cs) = dnf-add (conj-meet c lnil) (dnf-norm cs)
dnf-canon : DNF → Bool
dnf-canon f = dnf-eq (dnf-norm f) f
dnf-nonconst : DNF → Bool
dnf-nonconst lnil = false
dnf-nonconst (lcons lnil cs) = false
dnf-nonconst (lcons (lcons l ls) cs) = true

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2: skeletons with dimensions, and path application on cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A context's skeleton lists its entries, newest first: a type's shape or a dimension.
-- Codes count both (de Bruijn indices over one context of term and dimension variables, lib/code.cub);
-- a dimension contributes a direction to the cube of the judgments over the context and nothing to a
-- vertex's environment.
-- (Entry and dims are defined with the contexts, above)
-- the diagonal of the newest direction of a cube over sk with the dimension that index k of sk names
-- (exchanging the newest direction outward past each nearer dimension); an index that names a term
-- entry or nothing has no dimension, and gives the face at 0 (the side condition of a neutral path
-- application excludes it, P2.6)
diag-sk : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
diag-sk lnil k X c = face0-l X c
diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X c =
  if weq k #0 then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c
diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk) k X c =
  if weq k #0 then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
-- the newest direction at a literal (i or ~i), the index shifted by o (the dimensions a connection
-- has put in front of the skeleton)
papp-lit : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-lit sk X o l c =
  if snd l then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c
  else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
-- at a conjunction l ∧ m ∧ …: the connection λ i j → p (i ∧ j), then j at the rest (over the skeleton
-- with i in front, indices one further), then i at l; the empty conjunction is 1
papp-conj-from : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (ms : Conj) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-conj-from sk X o l lnil c = papp-lit sk X o l c
papp-conj-from sk X o l (lcons m ms) c =
  papp-lit sk X o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
papp-conj : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (c : Conj) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-conj sk X o lnil c = cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face1-l X) c
papp-conj sk X o (lcons l ls) c = papp-conj-from sk X o l ls c
-- at a disjunction: the connection λ i j → p (i ∨ j), likewise; the empty disjunction is 0
papp-dnf-from : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (c : Conj) (ds : DNF) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-dnf-from sk X o c lnil p = papp-conj sk X o c p
papp-dnf-from sk X o c (lcons d ds) p =
  papp-conj sk X o c (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) p))
-- a cube over sk with one more (newest) direction, at an interval element in canonical form over sk
papp-cube : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (f : DNF) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-cube sk X lnil p = cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) p
papp-cube sk X (lcons c cs) p = papp-dnf-from sk X #0 c cs p

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.1: cubes in a family over a cube
-- (2026-11-12) A line over a line L of X in a family Y: a point over each end and a path over L; a
-- cube over a cube likewise, one direction at a time (newest innermost, as Cube).
LineO : (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) → Line X → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
LineO X Y L = (ly0 : Y (fst L)) × (ly1 : Y (fst (snd L))) × PathP (λ i → Y (snd (snd L) i)) ly0 ly1
DCube : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) → Cube n X → Type 1
DCube zero X Y c = Y c
DCube (suc n) X Y c = DCube n (Line X) (LineO X Y) c
lineo-map : (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) (Z : Type 1) → ((x : X) → Y x → Z) → (L : Line X) → LineO X Y L → Line Z
lineo-map X Y Z f L D = (f (fst L) (fst D) , f (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) , λ i → f (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i))
-- a map out of a cube with a cube over it
dcube-map : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) (Z : Type 1) → ((x : X) → Y x → Z) → (c : Cube n X) → DCube n X Y c → Cube n Z
dcube-map zero X Y Z f c d = f c d
dcube-map (suc n) X Y Z f c d = dcube-map n (Line X) (LineO X Y) (Line Z) (lineo-map X Y Z f) c d
-- the cube over a cube given by a section of the family
lineo-of : (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → Y x) → (L : Line X) → LineO X Y L
lineo-of X Y f L = (f (fst L) , f (fst (snd L)) , λ i → f (snd (snd L) i))
dcube-of : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → Y x) → (c : Cube n X) → DCube n X Y c
dcube-of zero X Y f c = f c
dcube-of (suc n) X Y f c = dcube-of n (Line X) (LineO X Y) (lineo-of X Y f) c
-- mapping out of a cube with the cube of a section is mapping out of the cube: a path by induction
dcube-map-of : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) (Z : Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → Z) (g : (x : X) → Y x) (c : Cube n X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (dcube-map n X Y Z f c (dcube-of n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f x (g x)) c)
dcube-map-of zero X Y Z f g c = λ i → f c (g c)
dcube-map-of (suc n) X Y Z f g c = dcube-map-of n (Line X) (LineO X Y) (Line Z) (lineo-map X Y Z f) (lineo-of X Y g) c

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.3: the semantic path type
-- (2026-11-12) A semantic PathP type over semantic types X with meanings E: a line of semantic types
-- and a point over each end; its meaning is the language's PathP over the line, judgmentally (the
-- clause of TyE for the path shape is this pair, P2.6).
PathS : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
PathS X E = (pL : Line X) × E (fst pL) × E (fst (snd pL))
PathE : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) → PathS X E → Type
PathE X E D = PathP (λ i → E (snd (snd (fst D)) i)) (fst (snd D)) (snd (snd D))
pathE-pathp : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) (A0 A1 : X) (A : PathP (λ i → X) A0 A1) (a0 : E A0) (a1 : E A1) →
  Path Type (PathE X E ((A0 , A1 , A) , a0 , a1)) (PathP (λ i → E (A i)) a0 a1)
pathE-pathp X E A0 A1 A a0 a1 = refl
-- a value of a path type is a line over its type's line, with the type's endpoints as its ends
path-line : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) (D : PathS X E) → PathE X E D →
  (y0 : E (fst (fst D))) × (y1 : E (fst (snd (fst D)))) × PathP (λ i → E (snd (snd (fst D)) i)) y0 y1
path-line X E D p = (p 0 , p 1 , p)
path-line-ends : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) (D : PathS X E) (p : PathE X E D) →
  Path (E (fst (fst D))) (fst (path-line X E D p)) (fst (snd D))
path-line-ends X E D p = refl

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6 foundation: maps of cubes over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A judgment over a context with dimensions is a cube of contexts G and a cube over G of
-- meanings (the head's decision of this date); these are the structural maps between such cubes, each
-- by recursion on the dimension through its line version, so each computes on constructors with no
-- path. Their composites agree only up to paths (as cube-comp).
-- the dependent eliminator of Bool into Type 1
bool-elim1 : (P : Bool → Type 1) → P true → P false → (b : Bool) → P b
bool-elim1 P t f true = t
bool-elim1 P t f false = f
-- composition and inversion of paths in a type at level 1 (PathP: t50)
pcat : (A : Type 1) (x y z : A) → PathP (λ i → A) x y → PathP (λ i → A) y z → PathP (λ i → A) x z
pcat A x y z p q = λ i → comp (λ j → A) (λ j → [ i = 0 ↦ x , i = 1 ↦ q j ]) (p i)
psym : (A : Type 1) (x y : A) → PathP (λ i → A) x y → PathP (λ i → A) y x
psym A x y p = λ i → p (~ i)
-- a fibrewise map
lineo-fmap : (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → F x → F' x) → (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO X F' L
lineo-fmap X F F' h L D = (h (fst L) (fst D) , h (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) , λ i → h (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i))
dcube-fmap : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → F x → F' x) → (c : Cube n X) → DCube n X F c → DCube n X F' c
dcube-fmap zero X F F' h c d = h c d
dcube-fmap (suc n) X F F' h c d = dcube-fmap n (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) c d
-- two cubes over one base combined fibrewise
lineo-zip : (X : Type 1) (F F' F2 : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → F x → F' x → F2 x) → (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO X F' L → LineO X F2 L
lineo-zip X F F' F2 h L D E =
  (h (fst L) (fst D) (fst E) , h (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) (fst (snd E)) , λ i → h (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i) (snd (snd E) i))
dcube-zip : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' F2 : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → F x → F' x → F2 x) → (c : Cube n X) →
  DCube n X F c → DCube n X F' c → DCube n X F2 c
dcube-zip zero X F F' F2 h c d e = h c d e
dcube-zip (suc n) X F F' F2 h c d e = dcube-zip n (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO X F2) (lineo-zip X F F' F2 h) c d e
-- reindexing along a map of the base
lineo-reidx : (X X' : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : X → X') → ((x : X) → F x → F' (f x)) →
  (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO X' F' (line-map X X' f L)
lineo-reidx X X' F F' f g L D = (g (fst L) (fst D) , g (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) , λ i → g (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i))
dcube-reidx : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : X → X') → ((x : X) → F x → F' (f x)) →
  (c : Cube n X) → DCube n X F c → DCube n X' F' (cube-map n X X' f c)
dcube-reidx zero X X' F F' f g c d = g c d
dcube-reidx (suc n) X X' F F' f g c d =
  dcube-reidx n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (line-map X X' f) (lineo-reidx X X' F F' f g) c d
-- onto a base extended by a cube over it (weakening: the new base is dcube-map f c d)
lineo-push : (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') →
  ((x : X) (y : Y x) → F x → F' (f x y)) → (L : Line X) (D : LineO X Y L) → LineO X F L → LineO X' F' (lineo-map X Y X' f L D)
lineo-push X X' Y F F' f g L D E =
  (g (fst L) (fst D) (fst E) , g (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) (fst (snd E)) , λ i → g (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i) (snd (snd E) i))
dcube-push : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') →
  ((x : X) (y : Y x) → F x → F' (f x y)) → (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) → DCube n X F c → DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d)
dcube-push zero X X' Y F F' f g c d e = g c d e
dcube-push (suc n) X X' Y F F' f g c d e =
  dcube-push n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-push X X' Y F F' f g) c d e
-- back from such an extended base (substitution: the old base's fibres from the new one's)
lineo-pull : (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') →
  ((x : X) (y : Y x) → F' (f x y) → F x) → (L : Line X) (D : LineO X Y L) → LineO X' F' (lineo-map X Y X' f L D) → LineO X F L
lineo-pull X X' Y F F' f g L D E =
  (g (fst L) (fst D) (fst E) , g (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) (fst (snd E)) , λ i → g (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i) (snd (snd E) i))
dcube-pull : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') →
  ((x : X) (y : Y x) → F' (f x y) → F x) → (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) → DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d) → DCube n X F c
dcube-pull zero X X' Y F F' f g c d e = g c d e
dcube-pull (suc n) X X' Y F F' f g c d e =
  dcube-pull n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-pull X X' Y F F' f g) c d e
-- the cube category's generators over their images on the base (face0-l … diag-l above)
face0-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → F (face0-l X L)
face0-o X F L D = fst D
face1-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → F (face1-l X L)
face1-o X F L D = fst (snd D)
degen-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (x : X) → F x → LineO X F (degen-l X x)
degen-o X F x y = (y , y , λ i → y)
rev-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO X F (rev-l X L)
rev-o X F L D = (fst (snd D) , fst D , λ i → snd (snd D) (~ i))
meet-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) (meet-l X L)
meet-o X F L D = ((fst D , fst D , λ j → fst D) , D , λ i → (fst D , snd (snd D) i , λ j → snd (snd D) (i ∧ j)))
join-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) (join-l X L)
join-o X F L D = (D , (fst (snd D) , fst (snd D) , λ j → fst (snd D)) , λ i → (snd (snd D) i , fst (snd D) , λ j → snd (snd D) (i ∨ j)))
exch-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (Q : Line (Line X)) → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) Q → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) (exch-l X Q)
exch-o X F Q D =
  ((fst (fst D) , fst (fst (snd D)) , λ i → fst (snd (snd D) i)) ,
   (fst (snd (fst D)) , fst (snd (fst (snd D))) , λ i → fst (snd (snd (snd D) i))) ,
   λ j → (snd (snd (fst D)) j , snd (snd (fst (snd D))) j , λ i → snd (snd (snd (snd D) i)) j))
diag-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (Q : Line (Line X)) → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) Q → LineO X F (diag-l X Q)
diag-o X F Q D = (fst (fst D) , fst (snd (fst (snd D))) , λ i → snd (snd (snd (snd D) i)) i)
-- path application at any interval form to a cube degenerate in its newest direction gives the cube
-- back (a path, by induction: each generator composed with the degeneracy is judgmentally the identity
-- or a degeneracy, and composites of cube maps are cube-comp). A context's cube is degenerate in the
-- direction a path λ binds, so this carries a dpapp's meaning back over its context (P2.6).
diag-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (diag-sk sk k X (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
diag-deg lnil k X G = λ i → G
diag-deg (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X G =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X)
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)
                  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G)
    (pcat (Cube (dims sk) X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))
          (cube-map (dims sk) X X (λ x → x) G) G
          (cube-comp (dims sk) X (Line X) X (face0-l X) (degen-l X) G) (cube-id (dims sk) X G))
    (diag-deg sk (%wsub k #1) X G) (weq k #0)
diag-deg (lcons e-dim sk) k X G =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X)
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G)
                  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X)
                         (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G))) G)
    (pcat (Cube (dims sk) (Line X)) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G))
          (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (λ x → x) G) G
          (cube-comp (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G) (cube-id (dims sk) (Line X) G))
    (pcat (Cube (dims sk) (Line X))
          (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X)
             (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G)))
          (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) G)) G
          (λ i → diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X)
                   (cube-comp (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G i))
          (diag-deg sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) G))
    (weq k #0)
-- a path between cube maps whose functions agree judgmentally after composition with the degeneracy
-- (the two composites of cube maps meeting at one cube map)
cube-comp2 : (n : Nat) (X Y Y' Z : Type 1) (f : Y → Z) (g : X → Y) (f' : Y' → Z) (g' : X → Y') (c : Cube n X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c))
cube-comp2 n X Y Y' Z f g f' g' c p =
  pcat (Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c))
    (pcat (Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c)
       (cube-comp n X Y Z f g c) p)
    (psym (Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) (cube-comp n X Y' Z f' g' c))
papp-lit-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-lit sk X o l (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-lit-deg sk X o l G =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X)
                 (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)
                  else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))) G)
    (diag-deg sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X G)
    (pcat (Cube (dims sk) X)
       (diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
       (diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
       (λ i → diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-comp (dims sk) X (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) (degen-l X) G i))
       (diag-deg sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X G))
    (snd l)
-- (the connections composed with the degeneracy are the double degeneracy, which is the newer
-- skeleton's degeneracy of the degenerate cube: cube-comp2 at a judgmental pointwise equation)
papp-conj-from-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (ms : Conj) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-conj-from sk X o l ms (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-conj-from-deg sk X o l lnil G = papp-lit-deg sk X o l G
papp-conj-from-deg sk X o l (lcons m ms) G =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X)
    (papp-lit sk X o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms
       (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))))
    (papp-lit sk X o l (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
    (λ i → papp-lit sk X o l
       (pcat (Cube (dims sk) (Line X))
          (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms
             (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
          (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms
             (cube-map (suc (dims sk)) X (Line X) (degen-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
          (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)
          (λ j → papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms
             (cube-comp2 (dims sk) X (Line X) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) (degen-l X) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) (degen-l X) G
                (λ k → cube-map (dims sk) X (Line (Line X)) (λ x → degen-l (Line X) (degen-l X x)) G) j))
          (papp-conj-from-deg (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) i))
    (papp-lit-deg sk X o l G)
papp-conj-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (c : Conj) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-conj sk X o c (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-conj-deg sk X o lnil G =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face1-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))
    (cube-map (dims sk) X X (λ x → x) G) G
    (cube-comp (dims sk) X (Line X) X (face1-l X) (degen-l X) G) (cube-id (dims sk) X G)
papp-conj-deg sk X o (lcons l ls) G = papp-conj-from-deg sk X o l ls G
papp-dnf-from-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (c : Conj) (ds : DNF) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-dnf-from sk X o c ds (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-dnf-from-deg sk X o c lnil G = papp-conj-deg sk X o c G
papp-dnf-from-deg sk X o c (lcons d ds) G =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X)
    (papp-conj sk X o c (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds
       (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))))
    (papp-conj sk X o c (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
    (λ i → papp-conj sk X o c
       (pcat (Cube (dims sk) (Line X))
          (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds
             (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
          (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds
             (cube-map (suc (dims sk)) X (Line X) (degen-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
          (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)
          (λ j → papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds
             (cube-comp2 (dims sk) X (Line X) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) (degen-l X) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) (degen-l X) G
                (λ k → cube-map (dims sk) X (Line (Line X)) (λ x → degen-l (Line X) (degen-l X x)) G) j))
          (papp-dnf-from-deg (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) i))
    (papp-conj-deg sk X o c G)
papp-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (f : DNF) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-cube sk X f (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-deg sk X lnil G =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))
    (cube-map (dims sk) X X (λ x → x) G) G
    (cube-comp (dims sk) X (Line X) X (face0-l X) (degen-l X) G) (cube-id (dims sk) X G)
papp-deg sk X (lcons c cs) G = papp-dnf-from-deg sk X #0 c cs G
-- path application on cubes over cubes: the same composite of generators as papp-cube, on the fibres
-- over the base's image (the case on a variable index is the dependent eliminator, since the base's
-- image is computed by the same case)
diag-sk-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (diag-sk sk k X c)
diag-sk-d lnil k X F c d = face0-o X F c d
diag-sk-d (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X F c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d)
    (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) X F c d) (weq k #0)
diag-sk-d (lcons e-dim sk) k X F c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO X F) (diag-l X) (diag-o X F) c d)
    (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d))
    (weq k #0)
papp-lit-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-lit sk X o l c)
papp-lit-d sk X F o l c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F
                 (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c
                  else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
    (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F c d)
    (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d))
    (snd l)
papp-conj-from-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (ms : Conj) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-conj-from sk X o l ms c)
papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l lnil c d = papp-lit-d sk X F o l c d
papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l (lcons m ms) c d =
  papp-lit-d sk X F o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
    (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d))
papp-conj-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (o : Word) (cj : Conj) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-conj sk X o cj c)
papp-conj-d sk X F o lnil c d = dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face1-l X) (face1-o X F) c d
papp-conj-d sk X F o (lcons l ls) c d = papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l ls c d
papp-dnf-from-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (o : Word) (cj : Conj) (ds : DNF) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj ds c)
papp-dnf-from-d sk X F o cj lnil c d = papp-conj-d sk X F o cj c d
papp-dnf-from-d sk X F o cj (lcons e es) c d =
  papp-conj-d sk X F o cj (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
    (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d))
papp-cube-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (f : DNF) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-cube sk X f c)
papp-cube-d sk X F lnil c d = dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d
papp-cube-d sk X F (lcons cj cs) c d = papp-dnf-from-d sk X F #0 cj cs c d

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6a: contexts and meanings over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A context over a skeleton is a cube of the skeleton's contexts, one direction per
-- dimension entry; a meaning over it with values in Z is a cube over that cube of maps from each
-- vertex's environments into Z. A term's values are TV s, a semantic type of shape s with an element.
CtxV : Lst Entry → Type 1
CtxV sk = fst (CtxE sk)
EnvV : (sk : Lst Entry) → CtxV sk → Type 1
EnvV sk γ = snd (CtxE sk) γ
FbE : (sk : Lst Entry) (Z : Type 1) → CtxV sk → Type 1
FbE sk Z γ = EnvV sk γ → Z
CCtx : Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
CCtx = (ccsk : Lst Entry) × Cube (dims ccsk) (CtxV ccsk)
Mean : CCtx → Type 1 → Type 1
Mean Γ Z = DCube (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (snd Γ)
fmapM : (Γ : CCtx) (Z Z' : Type 1) → (Z → Z') → Mean Γ Z → Mean Γ Z'
fmapM Γ Z Z' h M = dcube-fmap (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (snd Γ) M
TV : TyShape → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
TV s = (tvA : Sem s) × El s tvA
-- Γ extended by a type that a meaning M over Γ gives at each vertex (f reads the type off M's value;
-- a λ's body's context is this at the λ's own conclusion, so no path is needed between them)
extM : (Γ : CCtx) (a : TyShape) (Y : Type 1) (f : (γ : CtxV (fst Γ)) → (EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Y) → EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Sem a) → Mean Γ Y → CCtx
extM Γ a Y f M =
  (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ) ,
   dcube-map (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Y) (CtxV (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ))) (λ γ e → (γ , f γ e)) (snd Γ) M)
-- Γ extended by a dimension: its cube degenerate in the new (newest) direction
dext : CCtx → CCtx
dext Γ = (lcons e-dim (fst Γ) , cube-map (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (Line (CtxV (fst Γ))) (degen-l (CtxV (fst Γ))) (snd Γ))
-- weakening a meaning to the extended contexts
wkM : (Γ : CCtx) (a : TyShape) (Y : Type 1) (f : (γ : CtxV (fst Γ)) → (EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Y) → EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Sem a) (M : Mean Γ Y)
  (Z : Type 1) → Mean Γ Z → Mean (extM Γ a Y f M) Z
wkM Γ a Y f M Z N =
  dcube-push (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (CtxV (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ))) (FbE (fst Γ) Y) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ)) Z)
    (λ γ e → (γ , f γ e)) (λ γ e N' ρ → N' (fst ρ)) (snd Γ) M N
dwkM : (Γ : CCtx) (Z : Type 1) → Mean Γ Z → Mean (dext Γ) Z
dwkM Γ Z N =
  dcube-reidx (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (Line (CtxV (fst Γ))) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (LineO (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z))
    (degen-l (CtxV (fst Γ))) (degen-o (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z)) (snd Γ) N

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6c: variables over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A variable of a skeleton: one of its term entries, by recursion on the skeleton (none:
-- the newest entry; some: one below it; a dimension entry is skipped). Its code's de Bruijn index
-- counts every entry; its shape and its meaning (a projection out of each vertex's environment) are
-- computed from it, so a variable judgment's meaning is the cube of that projection over the context.
VarP : Lst Entry → Type
VarP lnil = Empty
VarP (lcons e-dim sk) = VarP sk
VarP (lcons (e-ty a) sk) = Opt (VarP sk)
var-shape : (sk : Lst Entry) → VarP sk → TyShape
var-shape lnil v = Empty-rec v
var-shape (lcons e-dim sk) v = var-shape sk v
var-shape (lcons (e-ty a) sk) none = a
var-shape (lcons (e-ty a) sk) (some v) = var-shape sk v
var-word : (sk : Lst Entry) → VarP sk → Word
var-word lnil v = Empty-rec v
var-word (lcons e-dim sk) v = %wsucc (var-word sk v)
var-word (lcons (e-ty a) sk) none = #0
var-word (lcons (e-ty a) sk) (some v) = %wsucc (var-word sk v)
varM : (sk : Lst Entry) (v : VarP sk) (γ : CtxV sk) → EnvV sk γ → TV (var-shape sk v)
varM lnil v γ ρ = Empty-rec v
varM (lcons e-dim sk) v γ ρ = varM sk v γ ρ
varM (lcons (e-ty a) sk) none γ ρ = (snd γ (fst ρ) , snd ρ)
varM (lcons (e-ty a) sk) (some v) γ ρ = varM sk v (fst γ) (fst ρ)
varCube : (Γ : CCtx) (v : VarP (fst Γ)) → Mean Γ (TV (var-shape (fst Γ) v))
varCube Γ v = dcube-of (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) (TV (var-shape (fst Γ) v))) (varM (fst Γ) v) (snd Γ)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6b: naturality of the maps of cubes over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) Composites of the structural maps agree with the map of the composite: paths, by
-- induction on the dimension (each line version composes judgmentally).
fmap-fmap : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' F2 : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (h' : (x : X) → F' x → F2 x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X F2 c) (dcube-fmap n X F' F2 h' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d)) (dcube-fmap n X F F2 (λ x y → h' x (h x y)) c d)
fmap-fmap zero X F F' F2 h h' c d = λ i → h' c (h c d)
fmap-fmap (suc n) X F F' F2 h h' c d =
  fmap-fmap n (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO X F2) (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (lineo-fmap X F' F2 h') c d
fmap-reidx : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (F' F2 : X' → Type 1) (f : X → X') (g : (x : X) → F x → F' (f x))
  (h : (x : X') → F' x → F2 x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' F2 (cube-map n X X' f c))
    (dcube-fmap n X' F' F2 h (cube-map n X X' f c) (dcube-reidx n X X' F F' f g c d)) (dcube-reidx n X X' F F2 f (λ x y → h (f x) (g x y)) c d)
fmap-reidx zero X X' F F' F2 f g h c d = λ i → h (f c) (g c d)
fmap-reidx (suc n) X X' F F' F2 f g h c d =
  fmap-reidx n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (LineO X' F2) (line-map X X' f) (lineo-reidx X X' F F' f g) (lineo-fmap X' F' F2 h) c d
reidx-fmap : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (F F2 : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F2 x) (f : X → X')
  (g : (x : X) → F2 x → F' (f x)) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' F' (cube-map n X X' f c))
    (dcube-reidx n X X' F2 F' f g c (dcube-fmap n X F F2 h c d)) (dcube-reidx n X X' F F' f (λ x y → g x (h x y)) c d)
reidx-fmap zero X X' F F2 F' h f g c d = λ i → g c (h c d)
reidx-fmap (suc n) X X' F F2 F' h f g c d =
  reidx-fmap n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X F) (LineO X F2) (LineO X' F') (lineo-fmap X F F2 h) (line-map X X' f) (lineo-reidx X X' F2 F' f g) c d
fmap-push : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' F2 : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X')
  (g : (x : X) (y : Y x) → F x → F' (f x y)) (h : (x : X') → F' x → F2 x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) (e : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' F2 (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d))
    (dcube-fmap n X' F' F2 h (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d) (dcube-push n X X' Y F F' f g c d e))
    (dcube-push n X X' Y F F2 f (λ x y z → h (f x y) (g x y z)) c d e)
fmap-push zero X X' Y F F' F2 f g h c d e = λ i → h (f c d) (g c d e)
fmap-push (suc n) X X' Y F F' F2 f g h c d e =
  fmap-push n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (LineO X' F2) (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-push X X' Y F F' f g)
    (lineo-fmap X' F' F2 h) c d e
push-fmap : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F F2 : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') (h : (x : X) → F x → F2 x)
  (g : (x : X) (y : Y x) → F2 x → F' (f x y)) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) (e : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d))
    (dcube-push n X X' Y F2 F' f g c d (dcube-fmap n X F F2 h c e)) (dcube-push n X X' Y F F' f (λ x y z → g x y (h x z)) c d e)
push-fmap zero X X' Y F F2 F' f h g c d e = λ i → g c d (h c e)
push-fmap (suc n) X X' Y F F2 F' f h g c d e =
  push-fmap n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X F2) (LineO X' F') (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-fmap X F F2 h)
    (lineo-push X X' Y F2 F' f g) c d e
fmap-pull : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F F2 : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X')
  (g : (x : X) (y : Y x) → F' (f x y) → F x) (h : (x : X) → F x → F2 x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) (e : DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d)) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X F2 c)
    (dcube-fmap n X F F2 h c (dcube-pull n X X' Y F F' f g c d e)) (dcube-pull n X X' Y F2 F' f (λ x y z → h x (g x y z)) c d e)
fmap-pull zero X X' Y F F2 F' f g h c d e = λ i → h c (g c d e)
fmap-pull (suc n) X X' Y F F2 F' f g h c d e =
  fmap-pull n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X F2) (LineO X' F') (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-pull X X' Y F F' f g)
    (lineo-fmap X F F2 h) c d e
-- a fibrewise map commutes with carrying a cube over a base along a path of bases (by the filler of
-- the transport)
fmap-transp : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (c0 c1 : Cube n X) (p : PathP (λ i → Cube n X) c0 c1)
  (d : DCube n X F c0) →
  PathP (λ j → DCube n X F' c1)
    (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c1 (comp (λ i → DCube n X F (p i)) (λ i → []) d))
    (comp (λ i → DCube n X F' (p i)) (λ i → []) (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c0 d))
fmap-transp n X F F' h c0 c1 p d =
  λ j → comp (λ i → DCube n X F' (p i))
    (λ i → [ j = 0 ↦ dcube-fmap n X F F' h (p i) (comp (λ k → DCube n X F (p (i ∧ k))) (λ k → [ i = 0 ↦ d ]) d) ])
    (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c0 d)
-- (2026-11-12) a fibrewise map commutes with reindexing along a map of the base whose fibre maps
-- commute with it pointwise (q, judgmental at each generator below: refl)
fmap-gen : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (G G' : X' → Type 1) (f : X → X')
  (g : (x : X) → F x → G (f x)) (g' : (x : X) → F' x → G' (f x)) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (h2 : (x : X') → G x → G' x)
  (q : PathP (λ i → (x : X) → F x → G' (f x)) (λ x y → h2 (f x) (g x y)) (λ x y → g' x (h x y))) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' G' (cube-map n X X' f c))
    (dcube-fmap n X' G G' h2 (cube-map n X X' f c) (dcube-reidx n X X' F G f g c d))
    (dcube-reidx n X X' F' G' f g' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d))
fmap-gen n X X' F F' G G' f g g' h h2 q c d =
  pcat (DCube n X' G' (cube-map n X X' f c))
    (dcube-fmap n X' G G' h2 (cube-map n X X' f c) (dcube-reidx n X X' F G f g c d))
    (dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (λ x y → h2 (f x) (g x y)) c d)
    (dcube-reidx n X X' F' G' f g' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d))
    (fmap-reidx n X X' F G G' f g h2 c d)
    (pcat (DCube n X' G' (cube-map n X X' f c))
       (dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (λ x y → h2 (f x) (g x y)) c d)
       (dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (λ x y → g' x (h x y)) c d)
       (dcube-reidx n X X' F' G' f g' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d))
       (λ i → dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (q i) c d)
       (psym (DCube n X' G' (cube-map n X X' f c))
          (dcube-reidx n X X' F' G' f g' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d)) (dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (λ x y → g' x (h x y)) c d)
          (reidx-fmap n X X' F F' G' h f g' c d)))
-- a fibrewise map commutes with path application on cubes over cubes (by the recursion of
-- papp-cube-d, each generator by fmap-gen)
fmap-diag-sk : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (diag-sk sk k X c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (diag-sk sk k X c) (diag-sk-d sk k X F c d))
    (diag-sk-d sk k X F' c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-diag-sk lnil k X F F' h c d = λ i → h (fst c) (fst d)
fmap-diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X F F' h c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
                 (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c)
                    (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d)
                       (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) X F c d) b))
                 (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F' (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
                    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F') F' (face0-l X) (face0-o X F') c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
                    (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) X F' c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)) b))
    (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) (LineO X F') F F' (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) (face0-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) h
       (λ i L D → h (fst L) (fst D)) c d)
    (fmap-diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X F F' h c d) (weq k #0)
fmap-diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk) k X F F' h c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F'
                    (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                     else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
                 (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h
                    (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                     else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))
                    (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F
                                   (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                                    else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO X F) (diag-l X) (diag-o X F) c d)
                       (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
                          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d))
                       b))
                 (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F'
                                (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                                 else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
                    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (LineO X F') (diag-l X) (diag-o X F') c
                       (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h c d))
                    (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F') (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F') c
                          (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h c d)))
                    b))
    (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (LineO X F) (LineO X F')
       (diag-l X) (diag-o X F) (diag-o X F') (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h)) (lineo-fmap X F F' h)
       (λ i Q D → lineo-fmap X F F' h (diag-l X Q) (diag-o X F Q D)) c d)
    (pcat (DCube (dims sk) (Line X) (LineO X F') (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
       (dcube-fmap (dims sk) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h)
          (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))
          (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d)))
       (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F') (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
          (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d)))
       (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F') (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F') c
             (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h c d)))
       (fmap-diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d))
       (λ i → diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F') (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
          (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F'))
             (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) (exch-o X F')
             (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h)) (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h))
             (λ j Q D → lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (exch-l X Q) (exch-o X F Q D)) c d i)))
    (weq k #0)
fmap-papp-lit : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (o : Word) (l : Lit)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-lit sk X o l c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-lit sk X o l c) (papp-lit-d sk X F o l c d))
    (papp-lit-d sk X F' o l c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp-lit sk X F F' h o l c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F'
                    (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
                 (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F'  h
                    (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c))
                    (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F
                                   (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
                       (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F c d)
                       (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
                          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d)) b))
                 (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F'
                                (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
                    (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
                    (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F') (LineO X F') (rev-l X) (rev-o X F') c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))) b))
    (fmap-diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F F' h c d)
    (pcat (DCube (dims sk) X F' (diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
       (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c))
          (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d)))
       (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
          (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d)))
       (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F') (LineO X F') (rev-l X) (rev-o X F') c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)))
       (fmap-diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F F' h (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d))
       (λ i → diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
          (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) (rev-o X F')
             (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (λ j L D → lineo-fmap X F F' h (rev-l X L) (rev-o X F L D)) c d i)))
    (snd l)
fmap-papp-conj-from : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (ms : Conj)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-conj-from sk X o l ms c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-conj-from sk X o l ms c) (papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l ms c d))
    (papp-conj-from-d sk X F' o l ms c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp-conj-from sk X F F' h o l lnil c d = fmap-papp-lit sk X F F' h o l c d
fmap-papp-conj-from sk X F F' h o l (lcons m ms) c d =
  pcat (DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-conj-from sk X o l (lcons m ms) c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-conj-from sk X o l (lcons m ms) c) (papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l (lcons m ms) c d))
    (papp-lit-d sk X F' o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
       (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
          (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d))))
    (papp-conj-from-d sk X F' o l (lcons m ms) c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
    (fmap-papp-lit sk X F F' h o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
       (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d)))
    (λ i → papp-lit-d sk X F' o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
       (pcat (DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F' (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)))
          (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
             (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
                (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d)))
          (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
                (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d)))
          (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F') (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F') c
                (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)))
          (fmap-papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X F F' h (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d))
          (λ j → papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F'))
                (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) (meet-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h))
                (λ k L D → lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (meet-l X L) (meet-o X F L D)) c d j)) i))
fmap-papp-conj : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (o : Word) (cj : Conj)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-conj sk X o cj c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-conj sk X o cj c) (papp-conj-d sk X F o cj c d))
    (papp-conj-d sk X F' o cj c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp-conj sk X F F' h o lnil c d =
  fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) (LineO X F') F F' (face1-l X) (face1-o X F) (face1-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) h
    (λ i L D → h (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D))) c d
fmap-papp-conj sk X F F' h o (lcons l ls) c d = fmap-papp-conj-from sk X F F' h o l ls c d
fmap-papp-dnf-from : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (o : Word) (cj : Conj) (ds : DNF)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj ds c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj ds c) (papp-dnf-from-d sk X F o cj ds c d))
    (papp-dnf-from-d sk X F' o cj ds c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp-dnf-from sk X F F' h o cj lnil c d = fmap-papp-conj sk X F F' h o cj c d
fmap-papp-dnf-from sk X F F' h o cj (lcons e es) c d =
  pcat (DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj (lcons e es) c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj (lcons e es) c) (papp-dnf-from-d sk X F o cj (lcons e es) c d))
    (papp-conj-d sk X F' o cj (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
       (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
          (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d))))
    (papp-dnf-from-d sk X F' o cj (lcons e es) c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
    (fmap-papp-conj sk X F F' h o cj (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
       (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d)))
    (λ i → papp-conj-d sk X F' o cj (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
       (pcat (DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F' (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)))
          (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
             (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
                (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d)))
          (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
                (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d)))
          (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F') (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (join-l X) (join-o X F') c
                (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)))
          (fmap-papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X F F' h (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d))
          (λ j → papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F'))
                (join-l X) (join-o X F) (join-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h))
                (λ k L D → lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (join-l X L) (join-o X F L D)) c d j)) i))
fmap-papp : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (f : DNF)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-cube sk X f c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-cube sk X f c) (papp-cube-d sk X F f c d))
    (papp-cube-d sk X F' f c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp sk X F F' h lnil c d =
  fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) (LineO X F') F F' (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) (face0-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) h
    (λ i L D → h (fst L) (fst D)) c d
fmap-papp sk X F F' h (lcons cj cs) c d = fmap-papp-dnf-from sk X F F' h #0 cj cs c d

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6d: judgments, normal forms and derivations over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) the path shape's semantic types are P2.3's, judgmentally (t50: PathP at Type 1)
sem-path : (a : TyShape) → PathP (λ i → Type 1) (Sem (s-path a)) (PathS (Sem a) (El a))
sem-path a = λ i → PathS (Sem a) (El a)
-- a judgment: a context over cubes, a shape, a raw code and a meaning over the context (each vertex's
-- environments to a semantic type of the shape with an element)
Jdg : Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
Jdg = (jΓ : CCtx) × (js : TyShape) × Code × Mean jΓ (TV js)
-- the rules' data, read pointwise, and the named projections that give their premises' and
-- conclusions' meanings (shared by NN, Der, CompS and reify)
AppV : TyShape → TyShape → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
AppV a b = (avT : Fam a b) × El (s-pi a b) avT × El a (fst avT)
app-f : (a b : TyShape) → AppV a b → TV (s-pi a b)
app-f a b q = (fst q , fst (snd q))
app-a : (a b : TyShape) → AppV a b → TV a
app-a a b q = (fst (fst q) , snd (snd q))
app-r : (a b : TyShape) → AppV a b → TV b
app-r a b q = (snd (fst q) (snd (snd q)) , fst (snd q) (snd (snd q)))
sig-1 : (a b : TyShape) → TV (s-sig a b) → TV a
sig-1 a b q = (fst (fst q) , fst (snd q))
sig-2 : (a b : TyShape) → TV (s-sig a b) → TV b
sig-2 a b q = (snd (fst q) (fst (snd q)) , snd (snd q))
CaseV : TyShape → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
CaseV sP = (cvB : One1) × (cvP : Bool → Sem sP) × (cvx : Bool) × El sP (cvP true) × El sP (cvP false)
case-x : (sP : TyShape) → CaseV sP → TV s-bool
case-x sP q = (fst q , fst (snd (snd q)))
case-t : (sP : TyShape) → CaseV sP → TV sP
case-t sP q = (fst (snd q) true , fst (snd (snd (snd q))))
case-f : (sP : TyShape) → CaseV sP → TV sP
case-f sP q = (fst (snd q) false , snd (snd (snd (snd q))))
case-r : (sP : TyShape) → CaseV sP → TV sP
case-r sP q =
  (fst (snd q) (fst (snd (snd q))) ,
   bool-elim (λ b → El sP (fst (snd q) b)) (fst (snd (snd (snd q)))) (snd (snd (snd (snd q)))) (fst (snd (snd q))))
bool-v : Bool → One1 → TV s-bool
bool-v b u = (u , b)
-- a λ's body: its context is extM at the λ's own conclusion X (the domain read off X), its meaning X
-- pushed over X, applied to the new variable
lam-dom : (sk : Lst Entry) (a b : TyShape) (γ : CtxV sk) → (EnvV sk γ → TV (s-pi a b)) → EnvV sk γ → Sem a
lam-dom sk a b γ e ρ = fst (fst (e ρ))
lam-ctx : (Γ : CCtx) (a b : TyShape) → Mean Γ (TV (s-pi a b)) → CCtx
lam-ctx Γ a b X = extM Γ a (TV (s-pi a b)) (lam-dom (fst Γ) a b) X
lam-body : (Γ : CCtx) (a b : TyShape) (X : Mean Γ (TV (s-pi a b))) → Mean (lam-ctx Γ a b X) (TV b)
lam-body Γ a b X =
  dcube-push (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (CtxV (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ))) (FbE (fst Γ) (TV (s-pi a b))) (FbE (fst Γ) (TV (s-pi a b)))
    (FbE (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ)) (TV b)) (λ γ e → (γ , lam-dom (fst Γ) a b γ e))
    (λ γ e e2 ρ → (snd (fst (e (fst ρ))) (snd ρ) , snd (e (fst ρ)) (snd ρ))) (snd Γ) X X
-- a path λ's body: over dext Γ, the conclusion X reindexed at the degeneracy, each vertex's path read
-- as the line of its (type, value) pairs (its ends are the path type's endpoints judgmentally)
plam-line : (sk : Lst Entry) (a : TyShape) (γ : CtxV sk) (e : EnvV sk γ → TV (s-path a)) →
  LineO (CtxV sk) (FbE sk (TV a)) (degen-l (CtxV sk) γ)
plam-line sk a γ e =
  ((λ ρ → (fst (fst (fst (e ρ))) , fst (snd (fst (e ρ))))) ,
   (λ ρ → (fst (snd (fst (fst (e ρ)))) , snd (snd (fst (e ρ))))) ,
   λ i ρ → (snd (snd (fst (fst (e ρ)))) i , snd (e ρ) i))
plam-body : (Γ : CCtx) (a : TyShape) → Mean Γ (TV (s-path a)) → Mean (dext Γ) (TV a)
plam-body Γ a X =
  dcube-reidx (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (Line (CtxV (fst Γ))) (FbE (fst Γ) (TV (s-path a))) (LineO (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) (TV a)))
    (degen-l (CtxV (fst Γ))) (plam-line (fst Γ) a) (snd Γ) X
-- carrying a cube over a base along a path of bases (the form fmap-transp is about)
carry : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (c0 c1 : Cube n X) → PathP (λ i → Cube n X) c0 c1 → DCube n X F c0 → DCube n X F c1
carry n X F c0 c1 p d = comp (λ i → DCube n X F (p i)) (λ i → []) d
-- the meaning of a path applied at a canonical form f: the path's body over dext Γ applied at f
-- (papp-cube-d), carried back over Γ along papp-deg
papp-mean : (Γ : CCtx) (a : TyShape) (f : DNF) → Mean Γ (TV (s-path a)) → Mean Γ (TV a)
papp-mean Γ a f P =
  carry (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) (TV a))
    (papp-cube (fst Γ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) f (snd (dext Γ))) (snd Γ) (papp-deg (fst Γ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) f (snd Γ))
    (papp-cube-d (fst Γ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) (TV a)) f (snd (dext Γ)) (plam-body Γ a P))
-- a path between meanings, as a named type: a PathP over a path λ in a constructor's field is refused
-- (t52; workaround: this definition, used by npapp and dpapp)
PathM : (Γ : CCtx) (Z : Type 1) → Mean Γ Z → Mean Γ Z → Type 1
PathM Γ Z M N = PathP (λ i → Mean Γ Z) M N
-- neutral and normal forms, one family (the kind in the index), η-long and redex-free: a neutral is
-- normal only at Bool; a path application is neutral only at a canonical non-constant form
-- constructor binders subscripted ₀: t46
data NN : (KJ : NK × Jdg) → Type 1 where
  nvar : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (v₀ : VarP (fst Γ₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , var-shape (fst Γ₀) v₀ , cvar (var-word (fst Γ₀) v₀) , varCube Γ₀ v₀))
  napp : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (AppV a₀ b₀)) (f₀ c₀ : Code) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , s-pi a₀ b₀ , f₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (AppV a₀ b₀) (TV (s-pi a₀ b₀)) (app-f a₀ b₀) R₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , a₀ , c₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (AppV a₀ b₀) (TV a₀) (app-a a₀ b₀) R₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , b₀ , capp f₀ c₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (AppV a₀ b₀) (TV b₀) (app-r a₀ b₀) R₀))
  nfst : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀))) (p₀ : Code) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , s-sig a₀ b₀ , p₀ , R₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , a₀ , cfst p₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀)) (TV a₀) (sig-1 a₀ b₀) R₀))
  nsnd : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀))) (p₀ : Code) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , s-sig a₀ b₀ , p₀ , R₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , b₀ , csnd p₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀)) (TV b₀) (sig-2 a₀ b₀) R₀))
  ncase : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (s₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (CaseV s₀)) (x₀ t₀ f₀ : Code) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , s-bool , x₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (CaseV s₀) (TV s-bool) (case-x s₀) R₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , s₀ , t₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (CaseV s₀) (TV s₀) (case-t s₀) R₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , s₀ , f₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (CaseV s₀) (TV s₀) (case-f s₀) R₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , s₀ , c-case t₀ f₀ x₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (CaseV s₀) (TV s₀) (case-r s₀) R₀))
  nne : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV s-bool)) (x₀ : Code) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , s-bool , x₀ , R₀)) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , s-bool , x₀ , R₀))
  ntrue : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (B₀ : Mean Γ₀ One1) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , s-bool , c-true , fmapM Γ₀ One1 (TV s-bool) (bool-v true) B₀))
  nfalse : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (B₀ : Mean Γ₀ One1) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , s-bool , c-false , fmapM Γ₀ One1 (TV s-bool) (bool-v false) B₀))
  nlam : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (X₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-pi a₀ b₀))) (c₀ : Code) →
    NN (k-nf , (lam-ctx Γ₀ a₀ b₀ X₀ , b₀ , c₀ , lam-body Γ₀ a₀ b₀ X₀)) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , s-pi a₀ b₀ , clam c₀ , X₀))
  npair : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀))) (c1₀ c2₀ : Code) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , a₀ , c1₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀)) (TV a₀) (sig-1 a₀ b₀) R₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , b₀ , c2₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀)) (TV b₀) (sig-2 a₀ b₀) R₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , s-sig a₀ b₀ , cpair c1₀ c2₀ , R₀))
  nplam : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ : TyShape) (X₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-path a₀))) (c₀ : Code) →
    NN (k-nf , (dext Γ₀ , a₀ , c₀ , plam-body Γ₀ a₀ X₀)) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , s-path a₀ , cplam c₀ , X₀))
  npapp : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ : TyShape) (P₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-path a₀))) (p₀ : Code) (f₀ : DNF) →
    isTrue (dnf-canon f₀) → isTrue (dnf-nonconst f₀) →
    (Y₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV a₀)) → PathM Γ₀ (TV a₀) (papp-mean Γ₀ a₀ f₀ P₀) Y₀ →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , s-path a₀ , p₀ , P₀)) → NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , a₀ , cpapp p₀ (dnf-code f₀) , Y₀))
-- typing derivations, the same rules without the kinds; path application at any canonical form
-- constructor binders subscripted ₀: t46
data Der : (J : Jdg) → Type 1 where
  dvar : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (v₀ : VarP (fst Γ₀)) →
    Der (Γ₀ , var-shape (fst Γ₀) v₀ , cvar (var-word (fst Γ₀) v₀) , varCube Γ₀ v₀)
  dapp : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (AppV a₀ b₀)) (f₀ c₀ : Code) →
    Der (Γ₀ , s-pi a₀ b₀ , f₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (AppV a₀ b₀) (TV (s-pi a₀ b₀)) (app-f a₀ b₀) R₀) →
    Der (Γ₀ , a₀ , c₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (AppV a₀ b₀) (TV a₀) (app-a a₀ b₀) R₀) →
    Der (Γ₀ , b₀ , capp f₀ c₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (AppV a₀ b₀) (TV b₀) (app-r a₀ b₀) R₀)
  dfst : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀))) (p₀ : Code) →
    Der (Γ₀ , s-sig a₀ b₀ , p₀ , R₀) → Der (Γ₀ , a₀ , cfst p₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀)) (TV a₀) (sig-1 a₀ b₀) R₀)
  dsnd : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀))) (p₀ : Code) →
    Der (Γ₀ , s-sig a₀ b₀ , p₀ , R₀) → Der (Γ₀ , b₀ , csnd p₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀)) (TV b₀) (sig-2 a₀ b₀) R₀)
  dcase : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (s₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (CaseV s₀)) (x₀ t₀ f₀ : Code) →
    Der (Γ₀ , s-bool , x₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (CaseV s₀) (TV s-bool) (case-x s₀) R₀) →
    Der (Γ₀ , s₀ , t₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (CaseV s₀) (TV s₀) (case-t s₀) R₀) →
    Der (Γ₀ , s₀ , f₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (CaseV s₀) (TV s₀) (case-f s₀) R₀) →
    Der (Γ₀ , s₀ , c-case t₀ f₀ x₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (CaseV s₀) (TV s₀) (case-r s₀) R₀)
  dtrue : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (B₀ : Mean Γ₀ One1) → Der (Γ₀ , s-bool , c-true , fmapM Γ₀ One1 (TV s-bool) (bool-v true) B₀)
  dfalse : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (B₀ : Mean Γ₀ One1) → Der (Γ₀ , s-bool , c-false , fmapM Γ₀ One1 (TV s-bool) (bool-v false) B₀)
  dlam : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (X₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-pi a₀ b₀))) (c₀ : Code) →
    Der (lam-ctx Γ₀ a₀ b₀ X₀ , b₀ , c₀ , lam-body Γ₀ a₀ b₀ X₀) → Der (Γ₀ , s-pi a₀ b₀ , clam c₀ , X₀)
  dpair : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (R₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀))) (c1₀ c2₀ : Code) →
    Der (Γ₀ , a₀ , c1₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀)) (TV a₀) (sig-1 a₀ b₀) R₀) →
    Der (Γ₀ , b₀ , c2₀ , fmapM Γ₀ (TV (s-sig a₀ b₀)) (TV b₀) (sig-2 a₀ b₀) R₀) →
    Der (Γ₀ , s-sig a₀ b₀ , cpair c1₀ c2₀ , R₀)
  dplam : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ : TyShape) (X₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-path a₀))) (c₀ : Code) →
    Der (dext Γ₀ , a₀ , c₀ , plam-body Γ₀ a₀ X₀) → Der (Γ₀ , s-path a₀ , cplam c₀ , X₀)
  dpapp : (Γ₀ : CCtx) (a₀ : TyShape) (P₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV (s-path a₀))) (p₀ : Code) (f₀ : DNF) →
    isTrue (dnf-canon f₀) →
    (Y₀ : Mean Γ₀ (TV a₀)) → PathM Γ₀ (TV a₀) (papp-mean Γ₀ a₀ f₀ P₀) Y₀ →
    Der (Γ₀ , s-path a₀ , p₀ , P₀) → Der (Γ₀ , a₀ , cpapp p₀ (dnf-code f₀) , Y₀)
-- typed codes (paper §6.1): Code(Γ, A) = Σ c. Der(Γ, c, A), the meaning carried with the derivation;
-- evaluation (6.1) is that meaning
TCode : CCtx → TyShape → Type 1
TCode Γ s = (c : Code) × (v : Mean Γ (TV s)) × Der (Γ , s , c , v)
teval : (Γ : CCtx) (s : TyShape) → TCode Γ s → Mean Γ (TV s)
teval Γ s t = fst (snd t)
-- normal and neutral forms are derivations, with the same code and meaning
embed : {KJ : NK × Jdg} → NN KJ → Der (snd KJ)
embed (nvar Γ v) = dvar Γ v
embed (napp Γ a b R f c nf na) = dapp Γ a b R f c (embed nf) (embed na)
embed (nfst Γ a b R p np) = dfst Γ a b R p (embed np)
embed (nsnd Γ a b R p np) = dsnd Γ a b R p (embed np)
embed (ncase Γ s R x t f nx nt nf) = dcase Γ s R x t f (embed nx) (embed nt) (embed nf)
embed (nne Γ R x nx) = embed nx
embed (ntrue Γ B) = dtrue Γ B
embed (nfalse Γ B) = dfalse Γ B
embed (nlam Γ a b X c nb) = dlam Γ a b X c (embed nb)
embed (npair Γ a b R c1 c2 n1 n2) = dpair Γ a b R c1 c2 (embed n1) (embed n2)
embed (nplam Γ a X c nb) = dplam Γ a X c (embed nb)
embed (npapp Γ a P p f cf nc Y q np) = dpapp Γ a P p f cf Y q (embed np)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6e (begun): substitutions over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) The dimension part of a substitution Δ → Γ is a map of the cube category given, as in
-- CCHM, by an interval form over Δ's skeleton for each dimension of Γ's (CMap; a world's forms are
-- variables). Its action on cubes: the constant cube at no dimension, then path application at each
-- form (papp-cube), newest innermost; on cubes over cubes likewise (papp-cube-d).
cube-const : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) → X → Cube n X
cube-const zero X x = x
cube-const (suc n) X x = cube-const n (Line X) (degen-l X x)
dcube-const : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (x : X) → F x → DCube n X F (cube-const n X x)
dcube-const zero X F x y = y
dcube-const (suc n) X F x y = dcube-const n (Line X) (LineO X F) (degen-l X x) (degen-o X F x y)
CMap : Lst Entry → Lst Entry → Type
CMap sk' lnil = Unit
CMap sk' (lcons (e-ty a) sk) = CMap sk' sk
CMap sk' (lcons e-dim sk) = CMap sk' sk × DNF
cmap-cube : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) → CMap sk' sk → (X : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) X → Cube (dims sk') X
cmap-cube sk' lnil σ X c = cube-const (dims sk') X c
cmap-cube sk' (lcons (e-ty a) sk) σ X c = cmap-cube sk' sk σ X c
cmap-cube sk' (lcons e-dim sk) σ X c = papp-cube sk' X (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c)
cmap-d : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (σ : CMap sk' sk) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (c : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  DCube (dims sk) X F c → DCube (dims sk') X F (cmap-cube sk' sk σ X c)
cmap-d sk' lnil σ X F c d = dcube-const (dims sk') X F c d
cmap-d sk' (lcons (e-ty a) sk) σ X F c d = cmap-d sk' sk σ X F c d
cmap-d sk' (lcons e-dim sk) σ X F c d =
  papp-cube-d sk' X F (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c) (cmap-d sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) (LineO X F) c d)
-- a substitution Δ → Γ: its dimension part, a cube over Δ's context cube of Γ's vertex contexts with
-- environment maps, and a path from the dimension part of Γ's cube to that cube's first projection
SubF : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) → CtxV sk' → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
SubF sk' sk γ' = (sfγ : CtxV sk) × (EnvV sk' γ' → EnvV sk sfγ)
sub-base : (Δ Γ : CCtx) → DCube (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (snd Δ) → Cube (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ))
sub-base Δ Γ S = dcube-map (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (λ γ' p → fst p) (snd Δ) S
Sub : CCtx → CCtx → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
Sub Δ Γ = (sbd : CMap (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) × (sbS : DCube (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (snd Δ)) ×
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ))) (cmap-cube (fst Δ) (fst Γ) sbd (CtxV (fst Γ)) (snd Γ)) (sub-base Δ Γ sbS)
-- its action on meanings: the dimension part, carried along the path (sub-carried), then pulled
-- back along the environment maps
sub-carried : (Δ Γ : CCtx) (Z : Type 1) (σ : Sub Δ Γ) → Mean Γ Z → DCube (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ)))
sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M =
  carry (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (cmap-cube (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (snd Γ)) (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ)))
    (snd (snd σ)) (cmap-d (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (snd Γ) M)
sub-pull : (Δ Γ : CCtx) (Z : Type 1) (S : DCube (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (snd Δ)) →
  DCube (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (sub-base Δ Γ S) → Mean Δ Z
sub-pull Δ Γ Z S E =
  dcube-pull (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Δ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z)
    (λ γ' p → fst p) (λ γ' p e ρ → e (snd p ρ)) (snd Δ) S E
subM : (Δ Γ : CCtx) (Z : Type 1) → Sub Δ Γ → Mean Γ Z → Mean Δ Z
subM Δ Γ Z σ M = sub-pull Δ Γ Z (fst (snd σ)) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M)
-- at no dimension, the dimension part is the identity judgmentally (P1's case)
cmap-zero : (sk' : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (x : X) → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk') X) (cmap-cube sk' lnil unit X x) (cube-const (dims sk') X x)
cmap-zero sk' X x = λ i → cube-const (dims sk') X x
-- (2026-11-12) a fibrewise map commutes with the constant cube and with the action of a dimension
-- part (next definitions (3); by fmap-papp at each form)
fmap-const : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (x : X) (y : F x) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X F' (cube-const n X x)) (dcube-fmap n X F F' h (cube-const n X x) (dcube-const n X F x y)) (dcube-const n X F' x (h x y))
fmap-const zero X F F' h x y = λ i → h x y
fmap-const (suc n) X F F' h x y = fmap-const n (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (degen-l X x) (degen-o X F x y)
fmap-cmap : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (σ : CMap sk' sk) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x)
  (c : Cube (dims sk) X) (d : DCube (dims sk) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk') X F' (cmap-cube sk' sk σ X c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk') X F F' h (cmap-cube sk' sk σ X c) (cmap-d sk' sk σ X F c d))
    (cmap-d sk' sk σ X F' c (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h c d))
fmap-cmap sk' lnil σ X F F' h c d = fmap-const (dims sk') X F F' h c d
fmap-cmap sk' (lcons (e-ty a) sk) σ X F F' h c d = fmap-cmap sk' sk σ X F F' h c d
fmap-cmap sk' (lcons e-dim sk) σ X F F' h c d =
  pcat (DCube (dims sk') X F' (papp-cube sk' X (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c)))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk') X F F' h (papp-cube sk' X (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c))
       (papp-cube-d sk' X F (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c) (cmap-d sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) (LineO X F) c d)))
    (papp-cube-d sk' X F' (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c)
       (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk')) X F F' h (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c) (cmap-d sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) (LineO X F) c d)))
    (papp-cube-d sk' X F' (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c)
       (cmap-d sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) (LineO X F') c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)))
    (fmap-papp sk' X F F' h (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c) (cmap-d sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) (LineO X F) c d))
    (λ i → papp-cube-d sk' X F' (snd σ) (cmap-cube sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) c)
       (fmap-cmap sk' sk (fst σ) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) c d i))
-- pulling back after a fibrewise map is pulling back along the composite (a path, by induction)
pull-fmap : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' F2 : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') (h : (x : X') → F' x → F2 x)
  (g : (x : X) (y : Y x) → F2 (f x y) → F x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) (e : DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d)) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X F c)
    (dcube-pull n X X' Y F F2 f g c d (dcube-fmap n X' F' F2 h (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d) e))
    (dcube-pull n X X' Y F F' f (λ x y z → g x y (h (f x y) z)) c d e)
pull-fmap zero X X' Y F F' F2 f h g c d e = λ i → g c d (h (f c d) e)
pull-fmap (suc n) X X' Y F F' F2 f h g c d e =
  pull-fmap n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (LineO X' F2) (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-fmap X' F' F2 h)
    (lineo-pull X X' Y F F2 f g) c d e
-- the action of a substitution commutes with a pointwise map of meanings (next definitions (3))
subM-fmap : (Δ Γ : CCtx) (Z Z' : Type 1) (h : Z → Z') (σ : Sub Δ Γ) (M : Mean Γ Z) →
  PathM Δ Z' (fmapM Δ Z Z' h (subM Δ Γ Z σ M)) (subM Δ Γ Z' σ (fmapM Γ Z Z' h M))
subM-fmap Δ Γ Z Z' h σ M =
  pcat (Mean Δ Z') (fmapM Δ Z Z' h (subM Δ Γ Z σ M))
    (dcube-pull (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Δ) Z') (FbE (fst Γ) Z)
       (λ γ' p → fst p) (λ γ' p e ρ → h (e (snd p ρ))) (snd Δ) (fst (snd σ)) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M))
    (subM Δ Γ Z' σ (fmapM Γ Z Z' h M))
    (fmap-pull (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Δ) Z) (FbE (fst Δ) Z') (FbE (fst Γ) Z)
       (λ γ' p → fst p) (λ γ' p e ρ → e (snd p ρ)) (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (snd Δ) (fst (snd σ)) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M))
    (pcat (Mean Δ Z')
       (dcube-pull (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Δ) Z') (FbE (fst Γ) Z)
          (λ γ' p → fst p) (λ γ' p e ρ → h (e (snd p ρ))) (snd Δ) (fst (snd σ)) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M))
       (sub-pull Δ Γ Z' (fst (snd σ))
          (dcube-fmap (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ))) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M)))
       (subM Δ Γ Z' σ (fmapM Γ Z Z' h M))
       (psym (Mean Δ Z')
          (sub-pull Δ Γ Z' (fst (snd σ))
             (dcube-fmap (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ))) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M)))
          (dcube-pull (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Δ) Z') (FbE (fst Γ) Z)
             (λ γ' p → fst p) (λ γ' p e ρ → h (e (snd p ρ))) (snd Δ) (fst (snd σ)) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M))
          (pull-fmap (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (SubF (fst Δ) (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Δ) Z') (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z')
             (λ γ' p → fst p) (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (λ γ' p e ρ → e (snd p ρ)) (snd Δ) (fst (snd σ)) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M)))
       (λ i → sub-pull Δ Γ Z' (fst (snd σ))
          (pcat (DCube (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ))))
             (dcube-fmap (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ))) (sub-carried Δ Γ Z σ M))
             (carry (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (cmap-cube (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (snd Γ)) (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ)))
                (snd (snd σ))
                (dcube-fmap (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (cmap-cube (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (snd Γ))
                   (cmap-d (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (snd Γ) M)))
             (sub-carried Δ Γ Z' σ (fmapM Γ Z Z' h M))
             (fmap-transp (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ))
                (cmap-cube (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (snd Γ)) (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ))) (snd (snd σ))
                (cmap-d (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (snd Γ) M))
             (λ j → carry (dims (fst Δ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (cmap-cube (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (snd Γ)) (sub-base Δ Γ (fst (snd σ)))
                (snd (snd σ))
                (fmap-cmap (fst Δ) (fst Γ) (fst σ) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (snd Γ) M j)) i)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6e (1): renaming interval forms
-- (2026-11-12, next definitions (1)) A renaming of forms applies a map of variables to every literal,
-- structurally (no normalization, so that path application at the renamed form is the renamed path
-- application, (4)). A map r of variables that preserves weq and wlt (a monotone injection) commutes
-- with every operation of dnf-norm, so it preserves canonicity; it preserves non-constancy
-- structurally. The renamings are those of order-preserving embeddings of skeletons (OPE, below).
lit-r : (Word → Word) → Lit → Lit
lit-r r l = (r (fst l) , snd l)
conj-r : (Word → Word) → Conj → Conj
conj-r r lnil = lnil
conj-r r (lcons l ls) = lcons (lit-r r l) (conj-r r ls)
dnf-r : (Word → Word) → DNF → DNF
dnf-r r lnil = lnil
dnf-r r (lcons c cs) = lcons (conj-r r c) (dnf-r r cs)
-- r preserves equality and order of variables
MonoW : (Word → Word) → Type
MonoW r = ((a b : Word) → weq (r a) (r b) ≡ weq a b) × ((a b : Word) → wlt (r a) (r b) ≡ wlt a b)
-- composition of paths in a type of level 0, its points explicit
pcat0 : (A : Type) (x y z : A) → x ≡ y → y ≡ z → x ≡ z
pcat0 A x y z p q = concat p q
-- a map out of a conditional (by cases on the condition)
if-map : (A B : Type) (f : A → B) (b : Bool) (x y : A) → f (if b then x else y) ≡ (if b then f x else f y)
if-map A B f b x y = bool-elim (λ c → f (if c then x else y) ≡ (if c then f x else f y)) (λ i → f x) (λ i → f y) b
lit-eq-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (l m : Lit) → lit-eq (lit-r r l) (lit-r r m) ≡ lit-eq l m
lit-eq-r r h l m = λ i → andB (fst h (fst l) (fst m) i) (bool-eq (snd l) (snd m))
lit-lt-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (l m : Lit) → lit-lt (lit-r r l) (lit-r r m) ≡ lit-lt l m
lit-lt-r r h l m = λ i →
  if snd h (fst l) (fst m) i then true else (if fst h (fst l) (fst m) i then andB (not (snd l)) (snd m) else false)
conj-ins-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (l : Lit) (c : Conj) → conj-ins (lit-r r l) (conj-r r c) ≡ conj-r r (conj-ins l c)
conj-ins-r r h l lnil = λ i → lcons (lit-r r l) lnil
conj-ins-r r h l (lcons m ms) =
  pcat0 Conj
    (conj-ins (lit-r r l) (conj-r r (lcons m ms)))
    (if lit-eq l m then lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)
     else (if lit-lt l m then lcons (lit-r r l) (lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)) else lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r (conj-ins l ms))))
    (conj-r r (conj-ins l (lcons m ms)))
    (λ i → if lit-eq-r r h l m i then lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)
           else (if lit-lt-r r h l m i then lcons (lit-r r l) (lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms))
                 else lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-ins-r r h l ms i)))
    (pcat0 Conj
       (if lit-eq l m then lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)
        else (if lit-lt l m then lcons (lit-r r l) (lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)) else lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r (conj-ins l ms))))
       (if lit-eq l m then conj-r r (lcons m ms) else conj-r r (if lit-lt l m then lcons l (lcons m ms) else lcons m (conj-ins l ms)))
       (conj-r r (conj-ins l (lcons m ms)))
       (λ i → if lit-eq l m then lcons (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)
              else sym (if-map Conj Conj (conj-r r) (lit-lt l m) (lcons l (lcons m ms)) (lcons m (conj-ins l ms))) i)
       (sym (if-map Conj Conj (conj-r r) (lit-eq l m) (lcons m ms)
               (if lit-lt l m then lcons l (lcons m ms) else lcons m (conj-ins l ms)))))
conj-meet-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (c d : Conj) → conj-meet (conj-r r c) (conj-r r d) ≡ conj-r r (conj-meet c d)
conj-meet-r r h lnil d = λ i → conj-r r d
conj-meet-r r h (lcons l ls) d = cong (conj-ins (lit-r r l)) (conj-meet-r r h ls d) ∙ conj-ins-r r h l (conj-meet ls d)
conj-has-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (l : Lit) (c : Conj) → conj-has (lit-r r l) (conj-r r c) ≡ conj-has l c
conj-has-r r h l lnil = λ i → false
conj-has-r r h l (lcons m ms) = λ i → if lit-eq-r r h l m i then true else conj-has-r r h l ms i
conj-sub-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (c d : Conj) → conj-sub (conj-r r c) (conj-r r d) ≡ conj-sub c d
conj-sub-r r h lnil d = λ i → true
conj-sub-r r h (lcons l ls) d = λ i → andB (conj-has-r r h l d i) (conj-sub-r r h ls d i)
conj-eq-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (c d : Conj) → conj-eq (conj-r r c) (conj-r r d) ≡ conj-eq c d
conj-eq-r r h lnil lnil = λ i → true
conj-eq-r r h lnil (lcons m ms) = λ i → false
conj-eq-r r h (lcons l ls) lnil = λ i → false
conj-eq-r r h (lcons l ls) (lcons m ms) = λ i → andB (lit-eq-r r h l m i) (conj-eq-r r h ls ms i)
conj-lt-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (c d : Conj) → conj-lt (conj-r r c) (conj-r r d) ≡ conj-lt c d
conj-lt-r r h lnil lnil = λ i → false
conj-lt-r r h lnil (lcons m ms) = λ i → true
conj-lt-r r h (lcons l ls) lnil = λ i → false
conj-lt-r r h (lcons l ls) (lcons m ms) = λ i →
  if lit-lt-r r h l m i then true else (if lit-eq-r r h l m i then conj-lt-r r h ls ms i else false)
dnf-any-sub-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (c : Conj) (f : DNF) → dnf-any-sub (conj-r r c) (dnf-r r f) ≡ dnf-any-sub c f
dnf-any-sub-r r h c lnil = λ i → false
dnf-any-sub-r r h c (lcons d ds) = λ i → if conj-sub-r r h d c i then true else dnf-any-sub-r r h c ds i
dnf-drop-sup-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (c : Conj) (f : DNF) → dnf-drop-sup (conj-r r c) (dnf-r r f) ≡ dnf-r r (dnf-drop-sup c f)
dnf-drop-sup-r r h c lnil = λ i → lnil
dnf-drop-sup-r r h c (lcons d ds) =
  (λ i → if conj-sub-r r h c d i then dnf-drop-sup-r r h c ds i else lcons (conj-r r d) (dnf-drop-sup-r r h c ds i)) ∙
  sym (if-map DNF DNF (dnf-r r) (conj-sub c d) (dnf-drop-sup c ds) (lcons d (dnf-drop-sup c ds)))
dnf-insert-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (c : Conj) (f : DNF) → dnf-insert (conj-r r c) (dnf-r r f) ≡ dnf-r r (dnf-insert c f)
dnf-insert-r r h c lnil = λ i → lcons (conj-r r c) lnil
dnf-insert-r r h c (lcons d ds) =
  (λ i → if conj-lt-r r h c d i then lcons (conj-r r c) (lcons (conj-r r d) (dnf-r r ds)) else lcons (conj-r r d) (dnf-insert-r r h c ds i)) ∙
  sym (if-map DNF DNF (dnf-r r) (conj-lt c d) (lcons c (lcons d ds)) (lcons d (dnf-insert c ds)))
dnf-add-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (c : Conj) (f : DNF) → dnf-add (conj-r r c) (dnf-r r f) ≡ dnf-r r (dnf-add c f)
dnf-add-r r h c f =
  (λ i → if dnf-any-sub-r r h c f i then dnf-r r f
         else (cong (dnf-insert (conj-r r c)) (dnf-drop-sup-r r h c f) ∙ dnf-insert-r r h c (dnf-drop-sup c f)) i) ∙
  sym (if-map DNF DNF (dnf-r r) (dnf-any-sub c f) f (dnf-insert c (dnf-drop-sup c f)))
dnf-norm-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (f : DNF) → dnf-norm (dnf-r r f) ≡ dnf-r r (dnf-norm f)
dnf-norm-r r h lnil = λ i → lnil
dnf-norm-r r h (lcons c cs) =
  (λ i → dnf-add (conj-meet-r r h c lnil i) (dnf-norm-r r h cs i)) ∙ dnf-add-r r h (conj-meet c lnil) (dnf-norm cs)
dnf-eq-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (f g : DNF) → dnf-eq (dnf-r r f) (dnf-r r g) ≡ dnf-eq f g
dnf-eq-r r h lnil lnil = λ i → true
dnf-eq-r r h lnil (lcons d ds) = λ i → false
dnf-eq-r r h (lcons c cs) lnil = λ i → false
dnf-eq-r r h (lcons c cs) (lcons d ds) = λ i → andB (conj-eq-r r h c d i) (dnf-eq-r r h cs ds i)
dnf-canon-r : (r : Word → Word) (h : MonoW r) (f : DNF) → dnf-canon (dnf-r r f) ≡ dnf-canon f
dnf-canon-r r h f = (λ i → dnf-eq (dnf-norm-r r h f i) (dnf-r r f)) ∙ dnf-eq-r r h (dnf-norm f) f
dnf-nonconst-r : (r : Word → Word) (f : DNF) → dnf-nonconst (dnf-r r f) ≡ dnf-nonconst f
dnf-nonconst-r r lnil = λ i → false
dnf-nonconst-r r (lcons lnil cs) = λ i → false
dnf-nonconst-r r (lcons (lcons l ls) cs) = λ i → true
-- equality and order of words at successors and zero (from their definitions by induction, std)
weq-ss : (a b : Word) → weq (%wsucc a) (%wsucc b) ≡ weq a b
weq-ss a b = pcat0 Bool (weq (%wsucc a) (%wsucc b)) (eqw a b) (weq a b) (sym (eqw≡weq (%wsucc a) (%wsucc b))) (eqw≡weq a b)
weq-0s : (b : Word) → weq #0 (%wsucc b) ≡ false
weq-0s b = sym (eqw≡weq #0 (%wsucc b))
weq-s0 : (a : Word) → weq (%wsucc a) #0 ≡ false
weq-s0 a = sym (eqw≡weq (%wsucc a) #0)
wlt-ss : (a b : Word) → wlt (%wsucc a) (%wsucc b) ≡ wlt a b
wlt-ss a b = pcat0 Bool (wlt (%wsucc a) (%wsucc b)) (ltw a b) (wlt a b) (sym (ltw≡wlt (%wsucc a) (%wsucc b))) (ltw≡wlt a b)
wlt-0s : (b : Word) → wlt #0 (%wsucc b) ≡ true
wlt-0s b = sym (ltw≡wlt #0 (%wsucc b))
wlt-s0 : (a : Word) → wlt (%wsucc a) #0 ≡ false
wlt-s0 a = sym (ltw≡wlt (%wsucc a) #0)
-- the successor is a monotone injection; so is a map extended by 0 ↦ 0 and n+1 ↦ r n + 1
mono-succ : (r : Word → Word) → MonoW r → MonoW (λ k → %wsucc (r k))
mono-succ r h =
  ((λ a b → pcat0 Bool (weq (%wsucc (r a)) (%wsucc (r b))) (weq (r a) (r b)) (weq a b) (weq-ss (r a) (r b)) (fst h a b)) ,
   (λ a b → pcat0 Bool (wlt (%wsucc (r a)) (%wsucc (r b))) (wlt (r a) (r b)) (wlt a b) (wlt-ss (r a) (r b)) (snd h a b)))
mono-id : MonoW (λ k → k)
mono-id = ((λ a b i → weq a b) , (λ a b i → wlt a b))
w-keep : (Word → Word) → Word → Word
w-keep r k = %welimP (λ v → Word) k #0 (λ n g → %wsucc (r n))
-- a property of a pair of words with its four cases at zero and successor
w-cases2 : (P : Word → Word → Type) → P #0 #0 → ((m : Word) → P #0 (%wsucc m)) → ((n : Word) → P (%wsucc n) #0) →
  ((n m : Word) → P (%wsucc n) (%wsucc m)) → (a b : Word) → P a b
w-cases2 P z0 zs sz ss a b =
  %welimP (λ v → (b : Word) → P v b) a
    (λ b → %welimP (λ v → P #0 v) b z0 (λ m g → zs m))
    (λ n g b → %welimP (λ v → P (%wsucc n) v) b (sz n) (λ m g' → ss n m)) b
mono-keep : (r : Word → Word) → MonoW r → MonoW (w-keep r)
mono-keep r h =
  (w-cases2 (λ a b → weq (w-keep r a) (w-keep r b) ≡ weq a b) (λ i → weq #0 #0)
     (λ m → pcat0 Bool (weq #0 (%wsucc (r m))) false (weq #0 (%wsucc m)) (weq-0s (r m)) (sym (weq-0s m)))
     (λ n → pcat0 Bool (weq (%wsucc (r n)) #0) false (weq (%wsucc n) #0) (weq-s0 (r n)) (sym (weq-s0 n)))
     (λ n m → pcat0 Bool (weq (%wsucc (r n)) (%wsucc (r m))) (weq n m) (weq (%wsucc n) (%wsucc m))
        (fst (mono-succ r h) n m) (sym (weq-ss n m))) ,
   w-cases2 (λ a b → wlt (w-keep r a) (w-keep r b) ≡ wlt a b) (λ i → wlt #0 #0)
     (λ m → pcat0 Bool (wlt #0 (%wsucc (r m))) true (wlt #0 (%wsucc m)) (wlt-0s (r m)) (sym (wlt-0s m)))
     (λ n → pcat0 Bool (wlt (%wsucc (r n)) #0) false (wlt (%wsucc n) #0) (wlt-s0 (r n)) (sym (wlt-s0 n)))
     (λ n m → pcat0 Bool (wlt (%wsucc (r n)) (%wsucc (r m))) (wlt n m) (wlt (%wsucc n) (%wsucc m))
        (snd (mono-succ r h) n m) (sym (wlt-ss n m))))
-- order-preserving embeddings of skeletons, as closed data: an embedding keeps or skips each entry of
-- the larger skeleton (ope-src), newest first; the kept ones are the smaller (ope-tgt). (Indexed by
-- the two skeletons, its clauses at wdone carry fording's transports, which do not reduce without
-- regularity, so ope-cube wdone would not be the identity judgmentally; tested 2026-11-12.)
data OPE = wdone | wskip (e : Entry) (w : OPE) | wkeep (e : Entry) (w : OPE)
ope-src : OPE → Lst Entry
ope-src wdone = lnil
ope-src (wskip e w) = lcons e (ope-src w)
ope-src (wkeep e w) = lcons e (ope-src w)
ope-tgt : OPE → Lst Entry
ope-tgt wdone = lnil
ope-tgt (wskip e w) = ope-tgt w
ope-tgt (wkeep e w) = lcons e (ope-tgt w)
-- its map of variable indices, a monotone injection
ope-var : OPE → Word → Word
ope-var wdone k = k
ope-var (wskip e w) k = %wsucc (ope-var w k)
ope-var (wkeep e w) k = w-keep (ope-var w) k
ope-mono : (w : OPE) → MonoW (ope-var w)
ope-mono wdone = mono-id
ope-mono (wskip e w) = mono-succ (ope-var w) (ope-mono w)
ope-mono (wkeep e w) = mono-keep (ope-var w) (ope-mono w)
-- renaming a form along an embedding; canonicity and non-constancy are kept
dnf-ren : OPE → DNF → DNF
dnf-ren w f = dnf-r (ope-var w) f
canon-ren : (w : OPE) (f : DNF) → isTrue (dnf-canon f) → isTrue (dnf-canon (dnf-ren w f))
canon-ren w f c = subst {lzero} {lzero} {Bool} {isTrue} (sym (dnf-canon-r (ope-var w) (ope-mono w) f)) c
nonconst-ren : (w : OPE) (f : DNF) → isTrue (dnf-nonconst f) → isTrue (dnf-nonconst (dnf-ren w f))
nonconst-ren w f c = subst {lzero} {lzero} {Bool} {isTrue} (sym (dnf-nonconst-r (ope-var w) f)) c

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6e (4, first part): path application commutes with embeddings
-- (2026-11-12, next definitions (4); the identity and embedding laws of (2) are its instances) The
-- action of an embedding w : sk ⊆ sk' on cubes (ope-cube) is structural: a skipped dimension is a
-- degeneracy, a kept one is kept. Path application at a variable k over sk (diag-sk) commutes with it
-- at ope-var w k (diag-ren), by induction on w; the steps are diag-sk at a successor (diag-ty-s,
-- diag-dim-s), its naturality in the base (diag-nat) and that of ope-cube (ope-nat).
wsub-s1 : (a : Word) → wsub (%wsucc a) #1 ≡ a
wsub-s1 a =
  pcat0 Word (wsub (%wsucc a) #1) (subw a #0) a (sym (subw≡wsub (%wsucc a) #1))
    (%welimP (λ v → subw v #0 ≡ v) a (λ i → #0) (λ n h i → %wsucc n))
diag-ty-s : (sk : Lst Entry) (s : TyShape) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk) (%wsucc k) X c) (diag-sk sk k X c)
diag-ty-s sk s k X c = λ i →
  if weq-s0 k i then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (wsub-s1 k i) X c
diag-dim-s : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims (lcons e-dim sk))) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk) (%wsucc k) X c)
    (diag-sk sk k (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))
diag-dim-s sk k X c = λ i →
  if weq-s0 k i then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
  else diag-sk sk (wsub-s1 k i) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
diag-nat : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X Y : Type 1) (g : X → Y) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) Y) (diag-sk sk k Y (cube-map (suc (dims sk)) X Y g c)) (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g (diag-sk sk k X c))
diag-nat lnil k X Y g c = λ i → g (fst c)
diag-nat (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X Y g c =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) Y)
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line Y) Y (face0-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c)
                  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) Y (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c))
                 (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c)))
    (cube-comp2 (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) X Y (face0-l Y) (line-map X Y g) g (face0-l X) c (λ i → cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) Y (λ L → g (fst L)) c))
    (diag-nat sk (%wsub k #1) X Y g c) (weq k #0)
diag-nat (lcons e-dim sk) k X Y g c =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (suc (dims sk)) Y)
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line Y)) (Line Y) (diag-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) c)
                  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line Y)) (Line (Line Y)) (exch-l Y)
                         (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) c)))
                 (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)
                   (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                    else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))))
    (cube-comp2 (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (Line X) (Line Y) (diag-l Y) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g))
       (line-map X Y g) (diag-l X) c (λ i → cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line Y) (λ Q → line-map X Y g (diag-l X Q)) c))
    (pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk)) Y)
       (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line Y)) (Line (Line Y)) (exch-l Y)
          (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) c)))
       (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g))
          (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
       (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
       (λ i → diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line Y)
          (cube-comp2 (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (exch-l Y) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g))
             (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) (exch-l X) c
             (λ j → cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (λ Q → exch-l Y (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) Q)) c) i))
       (diag-nat sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
    (weq k #0)
-- the action of an embedding on cubes: a skipped dimension degenerate, a kept one kept; one step,
-- by cases on the entry, for any action f of the rest (skip-cube, keep-cube), so that each lemma
-- below is one step for any f with the property, then an induction on the embedding
skip-cube : (e : Entry) (sk' : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk') X → Cube (dims (lcons e sk')) X
skip-cube (e-ty s) sk' X c = c
skip-cube e-dim sk' X c = cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) c
keep-cube : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) → ((Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) →
  (X : Type 1) → Cube (dims (lcons e sk)) X → Cube (dims (lcons e sk')) X
keep-cube (e-ty s) sk' sk f X c = f X c
keep-cube e-dim sk' sk f X c = f (Line X) c
ope-cube : (w : OPE) (X : Type 1) → Cube (dims (ope-tgt w)) X → Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X
ope-cube wdone X c = c
ope-cube (wskip e w) X c = skip-cube e (ope-src w) X (ope-cube w X c)
ope-cube (wkeep e w) X c = keep-cube e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (λ Y → ope-cube w Y) X c
-- naturality in the base, one step for an action f natural in it, then by induction on w
CubeNat : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) → ((Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) → Type 2
CubeNat sk' sk f = (X Y : Type 1) (g : X → Y) (c : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk') Y) (f Y (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g c)) (cube-map (dims sk') X Y g (f X c))
skip-nat : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (f : (Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) → CubeNat sk' sk f →
  CubeNat (lcons e sk') sk (λ Y c → skip-cube e sk' Y (f Y c))
skip-nat (e-ty s) sk' sk f fn X Y g c = fn X Y g c
skip-nat e-dim sk' sk f fn X Y g c =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk') (Line Y))
    (cube-map (dims sk') Y (Line Y) (degen-l Y) (f Y (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g c)))
    (cube-map (dims sk') Y (Line Y) (degen-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk') X Y g (f X c)))
    (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) (cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (f X c)))
    (λ i → cube-map (dims sk') Y (Line Y) (degen-l Y) (fn X Y g c i))
    (cube-comp2 (dims sk') X Y (Line X) (Line Y) (degen-l Y) g (line-map X Y g) (degen-l X) (f X c)
       (λ i → cube-map (dims sk') X (Line Y) (λ x → degen-l Y (g x)) (f X c)))
keep-nat : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (f : (Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) → CubeNat sk' sk f →
  CubeNat (lcons e sk') (lcons e sk) (keep-cube e sk' sk f)
keep-nat (e-ty s) sk' sk f fn X Y g c = fn X Y g c
keep-nat e-dim sk' sk f fn X Y g c = fn (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c
ope-nat : (w : OPE) → CubeNat (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-cube w)
ope-nat wdone X Y g c = λ i → g c
ope-nat (wskip e w) X Y g c = skip-nat e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-cube w) (ope-nat w) X Y g c
ope-nat (wkeep e w) X Y g c = keep-nat e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-cube w) (ope-nat w) X Y g c
-- path application at a variable commutes with an embedding's action: one step for an action f
-- natural in the base with variable map r, then by induction on w
DiagRen : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) → (Word → Word) → ((Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) → Type 2
DiagRen sk' sk r f = (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk') X) (diag-sk sk' (r k) X (f (Line X) c)) (f X (diag-sk sk k X c))
skip-diag : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (r : Word → Word) (f : (Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) →
  DiagRen sk' sk r f → DiagRen (lcons e sk') sk (λ k → %wsucc (r k)) (λ Y c → skip-cube e sk' Y (f Y c))
skip-diag (e-ty s) sk' sk r f ih k X c =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk') X) (diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk') (%wsucc (r k)) X (f (Line X) c))
    (diag-sk sk' (r k) X (f (Line X) c)) (f X (diag-sk sk k X c))
    (diag-ty-s sk' s (r k) X (f (Line X) c)) (ih k X c)
skip-diag e-dim sk' sk r f ih k X c =
  pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X)
    (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk') (%wsucc (r k)) X (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (f (Line X) c)))
    (diag-sk sk' (r k) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk') (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X)
       (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (f (Line X) c))))
    (cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (f X (diag-sk sk k X c)))
    (diag-dim-s sk' (r k) X (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (f (Line X) c)))
    (pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X)
       (diag-sk sk' (r k) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk') (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X)
          (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (f (Line X) c))))
       (diag-sk sk' (r k) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) (f (Line X) c)))
       (cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (f X (diag-sk sk k X c)))
       (λ i → diag-sk sk' (r k) (Line X)
          (cube-comp (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) (degen-l (Line X)) (f (Line X) c) i))
       (pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X)
          (diag-sk sk' (r k) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) (f (Line X) c)))
          (cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (diag-sk sk' (r k) X (f (Line X) c)))
          (cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (f X (diag-sk sk k X c)))
          (diag-nat sk' (r k) X (Line X) (degen-l X) (f (Line X) c))
          (λ i → cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (ih k X c i))))
keep-diag : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (r : Word → Word) (f : (Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) →
  CubeNat sk' sk f → DiagRen sk' sk r f → DiagRen (lcons e sk') (lcons e sk) (w-keep r) (keep-cube e sk' sk f)
keep-diag (e-ty s) sk' sk r f fn ih k X c =
  %welimP (λ v → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk') X) (diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk') (w-keep r v) X (f (Line X) c))
                    (f X (diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk) v X c))) k
    (psym (Cube (dims sk') X) (f X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c))
       (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) X (face0-l X) (f (Line X) c)) (fn (Line X) X (face0-l X) c))
    (λ n h → pcat (Cube (dims sk') X) (diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk') (%wsucc (r n)) X (f (Line X) c))
       (f X (diag-sk sk n X c)) (f X (diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk) (%wsucc n) X c))
       (skip-diag (e-ty s) sk' sk r f ih n X c)
       (λ i → f X (diag-ty-s sk s n X c (~ i))))
keep-diag e-dim sk' sk r f fn ih k X c =
  %welimP (λ v → PathP (λ i → Cube (suc (dims sk')) X) (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk') (w-keep r v) X (f (Line (Line X)) c))
                    (f (Line X) (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk) v X c))) k
    (psym (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X) (f (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c))
       (cube-map (dims sk') (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (f (Line (Line X)) c)) (fn (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c))
    (λ n h → pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X) (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk') (%wsucc (r n)) X (f (Line (Line X)) c))
       (f (Line X) (diag-sk sk n (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
       (f (Line X) (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk) (%wsucc n) X c))
       (pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X) (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk') (%wsucc (r n)) X (f (Line (Line X)) c))
          (diag-sk sk' (r n) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk') (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) (f (Line (Line X)) c)))
          (f (Line X) (diag-sk sk n (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
          (diag-dim-s sk' (r n) X (f (Line (Line X)) c))
          (pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X)
             (diag-sk sk' (r n) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk') (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) (f (Line (Line X)) c)))
             (diag-sk sk' (r n) (Line X) (f (Line (Line X)) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
             (f (Line X) (diag-sk sk n (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
             (λ i → diag-sk sk' (r n) (Line X) (fn (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c (~ i)))
             (ih n (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))))
       (λ i → f (Line X) (diag-dim-s sk n X c (~ i))))
diag-ren : (w : OPE) → DiagRen (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-var w) (ope-cube w)
diag-ren wdone k X c = λ i → fst c
diag-ren (wskip e w) k X c = skip-diag e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-var w) (ope-cube w) (diag-ren w) k X c
diag-ren (wkeep e w) k X c = keep-diag e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-var w) (ope-cube w) (ope-nat w) (diag-ren w) k X c
-- path application at a renamed form commutes with an embedding's action (next definitions (4),
-- papp-ren), by the recursion of papp-cube: under a connection the skeleton has one more dimension
-- in front (kept), and the index of a literal is offset by o; hr says the embedding at hand renames
-- an offset index as r does the form's
wadd-0 : (k : Word) → %wadd k #0 ≡ k
wadd-0 k = sym (plusw≡wadd k #0)
wadd-s : (k o : Word) → %wadd k (%wsucc o) ≡ %wsucc (%wadd k o)
wadd-s k o = pcat0 Word (%wadd k (%wsucc o)) (%wsucc (plusw k o)) (%wsucc (%wadd k o)) (sym (plusw≡wadd k (%wsucc o))) (λ i → %wsucc (plusw≡wadd k o i))
RenAt : OPE → (Word → Word) → Word → Type
RenAt w r o = (k : Word) → ope-var w (%wadd k o) ≡ %wadd (r k) o
renat-keep : (w : OPE) (r : Word → Word) (o : Word) → RenAt w r o → RenAt (wkeep e-dim w) r (%wsucc o)
renat-keep w r o hr k =
  pcat0 Word (w-keep (ope-var w) (%wadd k (%wsucc o))) (%wsucc (%wadd (r k) o)) (%wadd (r k) (%wsucc o))
    (pcat0 Word (w-keep (ope-var w) (%wadd k (%wsucc o))) (%wsucc (ope-var w (%wadd k o))) (%wsucc (%wadd (r k) o))
       (λ i → w-keep (ope-var w) (wadd-s k o i)) (λ i → %wsucc (hr k i)))
    (sym (wadd-s (r k) o))
renat-0 : (w : OPE) → RenAt w (ope-var w) #0
renat-0 w k = pcat0 Word (ope-var w (%wadd k #0)) (ope-var w k) (%wadd (ope-var w k) #0) (λ i → ope-var w (wadd-0 k i)) (sym (wadd-0 (ope-var w k)))
papp-lit-ren : (w : OPE) (r : Word → Word) (o : Word) → RenAt w r o → (l : Lit) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims (ope-tgt w))) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X) (papp-lit (ope-src w) X o (lit-r r l) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (ope-cube w X (papp-lit (ope-tgt w) X o l c))
papp-lit-ren w r o hr l X c =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X)
                 (if b then diag-sk (ope-src w) (%wadd (r (fst l)) o) X (ope-cube w (Line X) c)
                  else diag-sk (ope-src w) (%wadd (r (fst l)) o) X (cube-map (dims (ope-src w)) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)))
                 (ope-cube w X (if b then diag-sk (ope-tgt w) (%wadd (fst l) o) X c
                                else diag-sk (ope-tgt w) (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c))))
    (pcat (Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X) (diag-sk (ope-src w) (%wadd (r (fst l)) o) X (ope-cube w (Line X) c))
       (diag-sk (ope-src w) (ope-var w (%wadd (fst l) o)) X (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (ope-cube w X (diag-sk (ope-tgt w) (%wadd (fst l) o) X c))
       (λ i → diag-sk (ope-src w) (hr (fst l) (~ i)) X (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (diag-ren w (%wadd (fst l) o) X c))
    (pcat (Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X)
       (diag-sk (ope-src w) (%wadd (r (fst l)) o) X (cube-map (dims (ope-src w)) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)))
       (diag-sk (ope-src w) (ope-var w (%wadd (fst l) o)) X (ope-cube w (Line X) (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
       (ope-cube w X (diag-sk (ope-tgt w) (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
       (λ i → diag-sk (ope-src w) (hr (fst l) (~ i)) X (ope-nat w (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c (~ i)))
       (diag-ren w (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
    (snd l)
papp-conj-from-ren : (w : OPE) (r : Word → Word) (o : Word) → RenAt w r o → (l : Lit) (ms : Conj) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims (ope-tgt w))) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X)
    (papp-conj-from (ope-src w) X o (lit-r r l) (conj-r r ms) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (ope-cube w X (papp-conj-from (ope-tgt w) X o l ms c))
papp-conj-from-ren w r o hr l lnil X c = papp-lit-ren w r o hr l X c
papp-conj-from-ren w r o hr l (lcons m ms) X c =
  pcat (Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X)
    (papp-lit (ope-src w) X o (lit-r r l) (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim (ope-src w)) X (%wsucc o) (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)
       (cube-map (dims (ope-src w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) (ope-cube w (Line X) c))))
    (papp-lit (ope-src w) X o (lit-r r l) (ope-cube w (Line X)
       (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim (ope-tgt w)) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))))
    (ope-cube w X (papp-conj-from (ope-tgt w) X o l (lcons m ms) c))
    (λ i → papp-lit (ope-src w) X o (lit-r r l)
       (pcat (Cube (suc (dims (ope-src w))) X)
          (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim (ope-src w)) X (%wsucc o) (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)
             (cube-map (dims (ope-src w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)))
          (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim (ope-src w)) X (%wsucc o) (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms)
             (ope-cube w (Line (Line X)) (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)))
          (ope-cube w (Line X) (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim (ope-tgt w)) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)))
          (λ j → papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim (ope-src w)) X (%wsucc o) (lit-r r m) (conj-r r ms) (ope-nat w (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c (~ j)))
          (papp-conj-from-ren (wkeep e-dim w) r (%wsucc o) (renat-keep w r o hr) m ms X (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)) i))
    (papp-lit-ren w r o hr l X (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim (ope-tgt w)) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)))
papp-conj-ren : (w : OPE) (r : Word → Word) (o : Word) → RenAt w r o → (cj : Conj) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims (ope-tgt w))) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X) (papp-conj (ope-src w) X o (conj-r r cj) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (ope-cube w X (papp-conj (ope-tgt w) X o cj c))
papp-conj-ren w r o hr lnil X c =
  psym (Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X) (ope-cube w X (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) X (face1-l X) c))
    (cube-map (dims (ope-src w)) (Line X) X (face1-l X) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (ope-nat w (Line X) X (face1-l X) c)
papp-conj-ren w r o hr (lcons l ls) X c = papp-conj-from-ren w r o hr l ls X c
papp-dnf-from-ren : (w : OPE) (r : Word → Word) (o : Word) → RenAt w r o → (cj : Conj) (ds : DNF) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims (ope-tgt w))) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X)
    (papp-dnf-from (ope-src w) X o (conj-r r cj) (dnf-r r ds) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (ope-cube w X (papp-dnf-from (ope-tgt w) X o cj ds c))
papp-dnf-from-ren w r o hr cj lnil X c = papp-conj-ren w r o hr cj X c
papp-dnf-from-ren w r o hr cj (lcons d ds) X c =
  pcat (Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X)
    (papp-conj (ope-src w) X o (conj-r r cj) (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim (ope-src w)) X (%wsucc o) (conj-r r d) (dnf-r r ds)
       (cube-map (dims (ope-src w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) (ope-cube w (Line X) c))))
    (papp-conj (ope-src w) X o (conj-r r cj) (ope-cube w (Line X)
       (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim (ope-tgt w)) X (%wsucc o) d ds (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))))
    (ope-cube w X (papp-dnf-from (ope-tgt w) X o cj (lcons d ds) c))
    (λ i → papp-conj (ope-src w) X o (conj-r r cj)
       (pcat (Cube (suc (dims (ope-src w))) X)
          (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim (ope-src w)) X (%wsucc o) (conj-r r d) (dnf-r r ds)
             (cube-map (dims (ope-src w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)))
          (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim (ope-src w)) X (%wsucc o) (conj-r r d) (dnf-r r ds)
             (ope-cube w (Line (Line X)) (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)))
          (ope-cube w (Line X) (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim (ope-tgt w)) X (%wsucc o) d ds (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)))
          (λ j → papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim (ope-src w)) X (%wsucc o) (conj-r r d) (dnf-r r ds) (ope-nat w (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c (~ j)))
          (papp-dnf-from-ren (wkeep e-dim w) r (%wsucc o) (renat-keep w r o hr) d ds X (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)) i))
    (papp-conj-ren w r o hr cj X (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim (ope-tgt w)) X (%wsucc o) d ds (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)))
papp-ren : (w : OPE) (f : DNF) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims (ope-tgt w))) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X) (papp-cube (ope-src w) X (dnf-ren w f) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (ope-cube w X (papp-cube (ope-tgt w) X f c))
papp-ren w lnil X c =
  psym (Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X) (ope-cube w X (cube-map (dims (ope-tgt w)) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c))
    (cube-map (dims (ope-src w)) (Line X) X (face0-l X) (ope-cube w (Line X) c)) (ope-nat w (Line X) X (face0-l X) c)
papp-ren w (lcons cj cs) X c = papp-dnf-from-ren w (ope-var w) #0 (renat-0 w) cj cs X c

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6e (2, first part): the dimension parts of worlds and of the identity
-- (2026-11-12, next definitions (2)) The dimension part sending dimension k of sk to the variable r k
-- of sk' (cmap-of). Its action: with a skipped entry in front of sk' and r one further (cmap-skip:
-- weakening by a type is the same cube, by a dimension the degenerate one), with a kept entry
-- (cmap-keep), the identity's (cmap-id) and an embedding's (cmap-ope: ope-cube).
cmap-of : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) → (Word → Word) → CMap sk' sk
cmap-of sk' lnil r = unit
cmap-of sk' (lcons (e-ty a) sk) r = cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))
cmap-of sk' (lcons e-dim sk) r = (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k)) , lcons (lcons (r #0 , true) lnil) lnil)
const-map : (n : Nat) (X Y : Type 1) (g : X → Y) (x : X) → PathP (λ i → Cube n Y) (cube-map n X Y g (cube-const n X x)) (cube-const n Y (g x))
const-map zero X Y g x = λ i → g x
const-map (suc n) X Y g x = const-map n (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) (degen-l X x)
skip-const : (e : Entry) (sk' : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (x : X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (lcons e sk')) X) (cube-const (dims (lcons e sk')) X x) (skip-cube e sk' X (cube-const (dims sk') X x))
skip-const (e-ty s) sk' X x = λ i → cube-const (dims sk') X x
skip-const e-dim sk' X x =
  psym (Cube (dims sk') (Line X)) (cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (cube-const (dims sk') X x)) (cube-const (dims sk') (Line X) (degen-l X x))
    (const-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) x)
-- path application at a variable is diag-sk there
papp-var : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (k : Word) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-cube sk X (lcons (lcons (k , true) lnil) lnil) c) (diag-sk sk k X c)
papp-var sk X k c = λ i → diag-sk sk (wadd-0 k i) X c
cmap-skip : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (r : Word → Word) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (lcons e sk')) X)
    (cmap-cube (lcons e sk') sk (cmap-of (lcons e sk') sk (λ k → %wsucc (r k))) X c) (skip-cube e sk' X (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) X c))
cmap-skip e sk' lnil r X c = skip-const e sk' X c
cmap-skip e sk' (lcons (e-ty a) sk) r X c = cmap-skip e sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k)) X c
cmap-skip e sk' (lcons e-dim sk) r X c =
  pcat (Cube (dims (lcons e sk')) X)
    (papp-cube (lcons e sk') X (lcons (lcons (%wsucc (r #0) , true) lnil) lnil)
       (cmap-cube (lcons e sk') sk (cmap-of (lcons e sk') sk (λ k → %wsucc (r (%wsucc k)))) (Line X) c))
    (diag-sk (lcons e sk') (%wsucc (r #0)) X (skip-cube e sk' (Line X) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c)))
    (skip-cube e sk' X (papp-cube sk' X (lcons (lcons (r #0 , true) lnil) lnil) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c)))
    (pcat (Cube (dims (lcons e sk')) X)
       (papp-cube (lcons e sk') X (lcons (lcons (%wsucc (r #0) , true) lnil) lnil)
          (cmap-cube (lcons e sk') sk (cmap-of (lcons e sk') sk (λ k → %wsucc (r (%wsucc k)))) (Line X) c))
       (papp-cube (lcons e sk') X (lcons (lcons (%wsucc (r #0) , true) lnil) lnil)
          (skip-cube e sk' (Line X) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c)))
       (diag-sk (lcons e sk') (%wsucc (r #0)) X (skip-cube e sk' (Line X) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c)))
       (λ i → papp-cube (lcons e sk') X (lcons (lcons (%wsucc (r #0) , true) lnil) lnil) (cmap-skip e sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k)) (Line X) c i))
       (papp-var (lcons e sk') X (%wsucc (r #0)) (skip-cube e sk' (Line X) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c))))
    (pcat (Cube (dims (lcons e sk')) X)
       (diag-sk (lcons e sk') (%wsucc (r #0)) X (skip-cube e sk' (Line X) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c)))
       (skip-cube e sk' X (diag-sk sk' (r #0) X (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c)))
       (skip-cube e sk' X (papp-cube sk' X (lcons (lcons (r #0 , true) lnil) lnil) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c)))
       (skip-diag e sk' sk' (λ k → k) (λ Y d → d) (λ k Y d i → diag-sk sk' k Y d) (r #0) X (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c))
       (λ i → skip-cube e sk' X (papp-var sk' X (r #0) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk (λ k → r (%wsucc k))) (Line X) c) (~ i))))
cmap-keep : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (r : Word → Word) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (dims (lcons e sk)) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (lcons e sk')) X)
    (cmap-cube (lcons e sk') (lcons e sk) (cmap-of (lcons e sk') (lcons e sk) (w-keep r)) X c) (keep-cube e sk' sk (λ Y → cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) Y) X c)
cmap-keep (e-ty s) sk' sk r X c = cmap-skip (e-ty s) sk' sk r X c
cmap-keep e-dim sk' sk r X c =
  pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X)
    (papp-cube (lcons e-dim sk') X (lcons (lcons (#0 , true) lnil) lnil)
       (cmap-cube (lcons e-dim sk') sk (cmap-of (lcons e-dim sk') sk (λ k → %wsucc (r k))) (Line X) c))
    (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk') #0 X (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c)))
    (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c)
    (pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X)
       (papp-cube (lcons e-dim sk') X (lcons (lcons (#0 , true) lnil) lnil)
          (cmap-cube (lcons e-dim sk') sk (cmap-of (lcons e-dim sk') sk (λ k → %wsucc (r k))) (Line X) c))
       (papp-cube (lcons e-dim sk') X (lcons (lcons (#0 , true) lnil) lnil)
          (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c)))
       (diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk') #0 X (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c)))
       (λ i → papp-cube (lcons e-dim sk') X (lcons (lcons (#0 , true) lnil) lnil) (cmap-skip e-dim sk' sk r (Line X) c i))
       (papp-var (lcons e-dim sk') X #0 (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c))))
    (pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk')) X)
       (cube-map (dims sk') (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c)))
       (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line X) (λ L → L) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c))
       (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c)
       (cube-comp (dims sk') (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (degen-l (Line X)) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c))
       (cube-id (dims sk') (Line X) (cmap-cube sk' sk (cmap-of sk' sk r) (Line X) c)))
cmap-id : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (dims sk) X) → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (cmap-cube sk sk (cmap-of sk sk (λ k → k)) X c) c
cmap-id lnil X c = λ i → c
cmap-id (lcons (e-ty s) sk) X c =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X) (cmap-cube (lcons (e-ty s) sk) (lcons (e-ty s) sk) (cmap-of (lcons (e-ty s) sk) (lcons (e-ty s) sk) (λ k → k)) X c)
    (cmap-cube sk sk (cmap-of sk sk (λ k → k)) X c) c (cmap-skip (e-ty s) sk sk (λ k → k) X c) (cmap-id sk X c)
cmap-id (lcons e-dim sk) X c =
  pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (cmap-cube (lcons e-dim sk) (lcons e-dim sk) (cmap-of (lcons e-dim sk) (lcons e-dim sk) (λ k → k)) X c)
    (cmap-cube sk sk (cmap-of sk sk (λ k → k)) (Line X) c) c (cmap-keep e-dim sk sk (λ k → k) X c) (cmap-id sk (Line X) c)
cmap-ope : (w : OPE) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube (dims (ope-tgt w)) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims (ope-src w)) X) (cmap-cube (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (cmap-of (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-var w)) X c) (ope-cube w X c)
cmap-ope wdone X c = λ i → c
cmap-ope (wskip e w) X c =
  pcat (Cube (dims (lcons e (ope-src w))) X) (cmap-cube (lcons e (ope-src w)) (ope-tgt w) (cmap-of (lcons e (ope-src w)) (ope-tgt w) (λ k → %wsucc (ope-var w k))) X c)
    (skip-cube e (ope-src w) X (cmap-cube (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (cmap-of (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-var w)) X c)) (ope-cube (wskip e w) X c)
    (cmap-skip e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-var w) X c) (λ i → skip-cube e (ope-src w) X (cmap-ope w X c i))
cmap-ope (wkeep e w) X c =
  pcat (Cube (dims (lcons e (ope-src w))) X)
    (cmap-cube (lcons e (ope-src w)) (lcons e (ope-tgt w)) (cmap-of (lcons e (ope-src w)) (lcons e (ope-tgt w)) (w-keep (ope-var w))) X c)
    (keep-cube e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (λ Y → cmap-cube (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (cmap-of (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-var w)) Y) X c) (ope-cube (wkeep e w) X c)
    (cmap-keep e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-var w) X c) (λ i → keep-cube e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (λ Y d → cmap-ope w Y d i) X c)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6e (2d, first part): the dependent forms over cubes
-- (2026-11-12, next definitions (2d)) subM acts on meanings by cmap-d, so each law of (2) and (4) on
-- cubes is needed on cubes over cubes: a PathP over the law on the base, by the same recursion.
-- Composites of paths over composites of base paths (pcat-d, psym-d; pcat-d by the filler of the base
-- pcat), reindexing along composites (reidx-comp, reidx-id, cube-comp2-d); the action of an embedding on
-- cubes over cubes (skip-d, keep-d, ope-cube-d: a skipped dimension degen-o, a kept one kept), its
-- naturality (ope-nat-d), diag-sk-d at a successor (diag-ty-s-d, diag-dim-s-d) and in the base
pcat-d : (A : Type 1) (B : A → Type 1) (x y z : A) (p : PathP (λ i → A) x y) (q : PathP (λ i → A) y z)
  (bx : B x) (b1 : B y) (bz : B z) → PathP (λ i → B (p i)) bx b1 → PathP (λ i → B (q i)) b1 bz →
  PathP (λ i → B (pcat A x y z p q i)) bx bz
pcat-d A B x y z p q bx b1 bz P Q = λ i →
  comp (λ j → B (comp (λ k → A) (λ k → [ i = 0 ↦ x , i = 1 ↦ q (j ∧ k) , j = 0 ↦ p i ]) (p i)))
    (λ j → [ i = 0 ↦ bx , i = 1 ↦ Q j ]) (P i)
psym-d : (A : Type 1) (B : A → Type 1) (x y : A) (p : PathP (λ i → A) x y) (bx : B x) (b1 : B y) →
  PathP (λ i → B (p i)) bx b1 → PathP (λ i → B (psym A x y p i)) b1 bx
psym-d A B x y p bx b1 P = λ i → P (~ i)
reidx-comp : (n : Nat) (X Y Z : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (G : Y → Type 1) (H : Z → Type 1) (f : Y → Z) (fd : (y : Y) → G y → H (f y))
  (g : X → Y) (gd : (x : X) → F x → G (g x)) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n Z H (cube-comp n X Y Z f g c i))
    (dcube-reidx n Y Z G H f fd (cube-map n X Y g c) (dcube-reidx n X Y F G g gd c d)) (dcube-reidx n X Z F H (λ x → f (g x)) (λ x y → fd (g x) (gd x y)) c d)
reidx-comp zero X Y Z F G H f fd g gd c d = λ i → fd (g c) (gd c d)
reidx-comp (suc n) X Y Z F G H f fd g gd c d =
  reidx-comp n (Line X) (Line Y) (Line Z) (LineO X F) (LineO Y G) (LineO Z H) (line-map Y Z f) (lineo-reidx Y Z G H f fd)
    (line-map X Y g) (lineo-reidx X Y F G g gd) c d
reidx-id : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X F (cube-id n X c i)) (dcube-reidx n X X F F (λ x → x) (λ x y → y) c d) d
reidx-id zero X F c d = λ i → d
reidx-id (suc n) X F c d = reidx-id n (Line X) (LineO X F) c d
cube-comp2-d : (n : Nat) (X Y Y' Z : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (G : Y → Type 1) (G' : Y' → Type 1) (H : Z → Type 1)
  (f : Y → Z) (fd : (y : Y) → G y → H (f y)) (g : X → Y) (gd : (x : X) → F x → G (g x))
  (f' : Y' → Z) (fd' : (y : Y') → G' y → H (f' y)) (g' : X → Y') (gd' : (x : X) → F x → G' (g' x)) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c)
  (p : PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c)) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n Z H (p i)) (dcube-reidx n X Z F H (λ x → f (g x)) (λ x y → fd (g x) (gd x y)) c d)
    (dcube-reidx n X Z F H (λ x → f' (g' x)) (λ x y → fd' (g' x) (gd' x y)) c d) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n Z H (cube-comp2 n X Y Y' Z f g f' g' c p i))
    (dcube-reidx n Y Z G H f fd (cube-map n X Y g c) (dcube-reidx n X Y F G g gd c d))
    (dcube-reidx n Y' Z G' H f' fd' (cube-map n X Y' g' c) (dcube-reidx n X Y' F G' g' gd' c d))
cube-comp2-d n X Y Y' Z F G G' H f fd g gd f' fd' g' gd' c d p pd =
  pcat-d (Cube n Z) (DCube n Z H) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c))
    (pcat (Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c)
       (cube-comp n X Y Z f g c) p)
    (psym (Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) (cube-comp n X Y' Z f' g' c))
    (dcube-reidx n Y Z G H f fd (cube-map n X Y g c) (dcube-reidx n X Y F G g gd c d))
    (dcube-reidx n X Z F H (λ x → f' (g' x)) (λ x y → fd' (g' x) (gd' x y)) c d)
    (dcube-reidx n Y' Z G' H f' fd' (cube-map n X Y' g' c) (dcube-reidx n X Y' F G' g' gd' c d))
    (pcat-d (Cube n Z) (DCube n Z H) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c)
       (cube-comp n X Y Z f g c) p
       (dcube-reidx n Y Z G H f fd (cube-map n X Y g c) (dcube-reidx n X Y F G g gd c d))
       (dcube-reidx n X Z F H (λ x → f (g x)) (λ x y → fd (g x) (gd x y)) c d)
       (dcube-reidx n X Z F H (λ x → f' (g' x)) (λ x y → fd' (g' x) (gd' x y)) c d)
       (reidx-comp n X Y Z F G H f fd g gd c d) pd)
    (psym-d (Cube n Z) (DCube n Z H) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) (cube-comp n X Y' Z f' g' c)
       (dcube-reidx n Y' Z G' H f' fd' (cube-map n X Y' g' c) (dcube-reidx n X Y' F G' g' gd' c d))
       (dcube-reidx n X Z F H (λ x → f' (g' x)) (λ x y → fd' (g' x) (gd' x y)) c d)
       (reidx-comp n X Y' Z F G' H f' fd' g' gd' c d))
skip-d : (e : Entry) (sk' : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (c : Cube (dims sk') X) →
  DCube (dims sk') X F c → DCube (dims (lcons e sk')) X F (skip-cube e sk' X c)
skip-d (e-ty s) sk' X F c d = d
skip-d e-dim sk' X F c d = dcube-reidx (dims sk') X (Line X) F (LineO X F) (degen-l X) (degen-o X F) c d
CubeD : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) → ((Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) → Type 2
CubeD sk' sk f = (Y : Type 1) (G : Y → Type 1) (c : Cube (dims sk) Y) → DCube (dims sk) Y G c → DCube (dims sk') Y G (f Y c)
keep-d : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (f : (Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) → CubeD sk' sk f →
  CubeD (lcons e sk') (lcons e sk) (keep-cube e sk' sk f)
keep-d (e-ty s) sk' sk f fd X F c d = fd X F c d
keep-d e-dim sk' sk f fd X F c d = fd (Line X) (LineO X F) c d
ope-cube-d : (w : OPE) → CubeD (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-cube w)
ope-cube-d wdone X F c d = d
ope-cube-d (wskip e w) X F c d = skip-d e (ope-src w) X F (ope-cube w X c) (ope-cube-d w X F c d)
ope-cube-d (wkeep e w) X F c d = keep-d e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-cube w) (ope-cube-d w) X F c d
CubeNatD : (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (f : (Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) → CubeD sk' sk f → CubeNat sk' sk f → Type 2
CubeNatD sk' sk f fd fn = (X Y : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (G : Y → Type 1) (g : X → Y) (gd : (x : X) → F x → G (g x))
  (c : Cube (dims sk) X) (d : DCube (dims sk) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk') Y G (fn X Y g c i))
    (fd Y G (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g c) (dcube-reidx (dims sk) X Y F G g gd c d)) (dcube-reidx (dims sk') X Y F G g gd (f X c) (fd X F c d))
skip-nat-d : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (f : (Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) (fd : CubeD sk' sk f)
  (fn : CubeNat sk' sk f) → CubeNatD sk' sk f fd fn →
  CubeNatD (lcons e sk') sk (λ Y c → skip-cube e sk' Y (f Y c)) (λ Y G c d → skip-d e sk' Y G (f Y c) (fd Y G c d))
    (skip-nat e sk' sk f fn)
skip-nat-d (e-ty s) sk' sk f fd fn fnd X Y F G g gd c d = fnd X Y F G g gd c d
skip-nat-d e-dim sk' sk f fd fn fnd X Y F G g gd c d =
  pcat-d (Cube (dims sk') (Line Y)) (DCube (dims sk') (Line Y) (LineO Y G))
    (cube-map (dims sk') Y (Line Y) (degen-l Y) (f Y (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g c)))
    (cube-map (dims sk') Y (Line Y) (degen-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk') X Y g (f X c)))
    (cube-map (dims sk') (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) (cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (f X c)))
    (λ i → cube-map (dims sk') Y (Line Y) (degen-l Y) (fn X Y g c i))
    (cube-comp2 (dims sk') X Y (Line X) (Line Y) (degen-l Y) g (line-map X Y g) (degen-l X) (f X c)
       (λ i → cube-map (dims sk') X (Line Y) (λ x → degen-l Y (g x)) (f X c)))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk') Y (Line Y) G (LineO Y G) (degen-l Y) (degen-o Y G) (f Y (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g c))
       (fd Y G (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g c) (dcube-reidx (dims sk) X Y F G g gd c d)))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk') Y (Line Y) G (LineO Y G) (degen-l Y) (degen-o Y G) (cube-map (dims sk') X Y g (f X c))
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk') X Y F G g gd (f X c) (fd X F c d)))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk') (Line X) (Line Y) (LineO X F) (LineO Y G) (line-map X Y g) (lineo-reidx X Y F G g gd)
       (cube-map (dims sk') X (Line X) (degen-l X) (f X c)) (dcube-reidx (dims sk') X (Line X) F (LineO X F) (degen-l X) (degen-o X F) (f X c) (fd X F c d)))
    (λ i → dcube-reidx (dims sk') Y (Line Y) G (LineO Y G) (degen-l Y) (degen-o Y G) (fn X Y g c i) (fnd X Y F G g gd c d i))
    (cube-comp2-d (dims sk') X Y (Line X) (Line Y) F G (LineO X F) (LineO Y G) (degen-l Y) (degen-o Y G) g gd (line-map X Y g) (lineo-reidx X Y F G g gd)
       (degen-l X) (degen-o X F) (f X c) (fd X F c d)
       (λ i → cube-map (dims sk') X (Line Y) (λ x → degen-l Y (g x)) (f X c))
       (λ i → dcube-reidx (dims sk') X (Line Y) F (LineO Y G) (λ x → degen-l Y (g x)) (λ x y → degen-o Y G (g x) (gd x y)) (f X c) (fd X F c d)))
keep-nat-d : (e : Entry) (sk' sk : Lst Entry) (f : (Y : Type 1) → Cube (dims sk) Y → Cube (dims sk') Y) (fd : CubeD sk' sk f)
  (fn : CubeNat sk' sk f) → CubeNatD sk' sk f fd fn →
  CubeNatD (lcons e sk') (lcons e sk) (keep-cube e sk' sk f) (keep-d e sk' sk f fd) (keep-nat e sk' sk f fn)
keep-nat-d (e-ty s) sk' sk f fd fn fnd X Y F G g gd c d = fnd X Y F G g gd c d
keep-nat-d e-dim sk' sk f fd fn fnd X Y F G g gd c d =
  fnd (Line X) (Line Y) (LineO X F) (LineO Y G) (line-map X Y g) (lineo-reidx X Y F G g gd) c d
ope-nat-d : (w : OPE) → CubeNatD (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-cube w) (ope-cube-d w) (ope-nat w)
ope-nat-d wdone X Y F G g gd c d = λ i → gd c d
ope-nat-d (wskip e w) X Y F G g gd c d =
  skip-nat-d e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-cube w) (ope-cube-d w) (ope-nat w) (ope-nat-d w) X Y F G g gd c d
ope-nat-d (wkeep e w) X Y F G g gd c d =
  keep-nat-d e (ope-src w) (ope-tgt w) (ope-cube w) (ope-cube-d w) (ope-nat w) (ope-nat-d w) X Y F G g gd c d



diag-ty-s-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (s : TyShape) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F (diag-ty-s sk s k X c i)) (diag-sk-d (lcons (e-ty s) sk) (%wsucc k) X F c d) (diag-sk-d sk k X F c d)
diag-ty-s-d sk s k X F c d = λ i →
  bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (wsub-s1 k i) X c))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d) (diag-sk-d sk (wsub-s1 k i) X F c d) (weq-s0 k i)
diag-dim-s-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims (lcons e-dim sk))) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims (lcons e-dim sk))) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F (diag-dim-s sk k X c i)) (diag-sk-d (lcons e-dim sk) (%wsucc k) X F c d)
    (diag-sk-d sk k (Line X) (LineO X F) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c) (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d))
diag-dim-s-d sk k X F c d = λ i →
  bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c else diag-sk sk (wsub-s1 k i) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO X F) (diag-l X) (diag-o X F) c d)
    (diag-sk-d sk (wsub-s1 k i) (Line X) (LineO X F) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c) (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d)) (weq-s0 k i)
diag-nat-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X Y : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (G : Y → Type 1) (g : X → Y) (gd : (x : X) → F x → G (g x))
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) Y G (diag-nat sk k X Y g c i))
    (diag-sk-d sk k Y G (cube-map (suc (dims sk)) X Y g c) (dcube-reidx (suc (dims sk)) X Y F G g gd c d))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) X Y F G g gd (diag-sk sk k X c) (diag-sk-d sk k X F c d))
diag-nat-d lnil k X Y F G g gd c d = λ i → gd (fst c) (fst d)
diag-nat-d (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X Y F G g gd c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) Y G
                   (bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) Y)
                       (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line Y) Y (face0-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c) else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) Y (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c))
                       (cube-map (dims sk) X Y g (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c)))
                     (cube-comp2 (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) X Y (face0-l Y) (line-map X Y g) g (face0-l X) c (λ i → cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) Y (λ L → g (fst L)) c))
                     (diag-nat sk (%wsub k #1) X Y g c) b i))
                 (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) Y G (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line Y) Y (face0-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c) else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) Y (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c)))
                    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line Y) Y (LineO Y G) G (face0-l Y) (face0-o Y G) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c) (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (LineO X F) (LineO Y G) (line-map X Y g) (lineo-reidx X Y F G g gd) c d)) (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) Y G (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) c) (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (LineO X F) (LineO Y G) (line-map X Y g) (lineo-reidx X Y F G g gd) c d)) b)
                 (dcube-reidx (dims sk) X Y F G g gd (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c)
                    (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d) (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) X F c d) b)))
    (cube-comp2-d (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) X Y (LineO X F) (LineO Y G) F G (face0-l Y) (face0-o Y G) (line-map X Y g) (lineo-reidx X Y F G g gd) g gd (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d
       (λ i → cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) Y (λ L → g (fst L)) c)
       (λ i → dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) Y (LineO X F) G (λ L → g (fst L)) (λ L D → gd (fst L) (fst D)) c d))
    (diag-nat-d sk (%wsub k #1) X Y F G g gd c d) (weq k #0)
diag-nat-d (lcons e-dim sk) k X Y F G g gd c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → DCube (suc (dims sk)) Y G
                   (bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (suc (dims sk)) Y)
                       (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line Y)) (Line Y) (diag-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) c) else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line Y)) (Line (Line Y)) (exch-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) c)))
                       (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)
                         (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))))
                     (cube-comp2 (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (Line X) (Line Y) (diag-l Y) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g))
                        (line-map X Y g) (diag-l X) c (λ i → cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line Y) (λ Q → line-map X Y g (diag-l X Q)) c))
                     (pcat (Cube (suc (dims sk)) Y) (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line Y)) (Line (Line Y)) (exch-l Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) c))) (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line Y) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
                        (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
                        (λ i → diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line Y)
                           (cube-comp2 (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (exch-l Y) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) (line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) (exch-l X) c
                              (λ j → cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line Y)) (λ Q → exch-l Y ((line-map (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g)) Q)) c) i))
                        (diag-nat sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y g) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))) b i))
